window.I18N_STRINGS = {"ru":{"Triple-click to hide the text":"Тройной клик скрывает текст","Show text":"Показать текст","Team Singularity":"Команда Singularity","Team Singularity · Team lead: Muzayana · Analyst · Engineer · Programmer":"Команда Singularity · Руководитель: Музаяна · Аналитик · Инженер · Программист","Pages":"Страницы","Missions":"Миссии","Explore":"Исследовать","Learn":"Учиться","Compare":"Сравнить","Glossary":"Словарь","Search the site":"Поиск по сайту","Search (Ctrl K)":"Поиск (Ctrl K)","Turn sound on":"Включить звук","Turn sound off":"Выключить звук","Sound off":"Звук выключен","Sound on":"Звук включён","Settings":"Настройки","Open navigation":"Открыть меню","Close navigation":"Закрыть меню","3D model of Perseverance. Drag, or use the arrow keys while focused, to turn it.":"3D-модель Perseverance. Перетащите или нажимайте стрелки, чтобы повернуть её.","The 3D model could not load, so you are seeing the NASA photo.":"3D-модель не загрузилась, поэтому показано фото NASA.","Try again":"Попробовать снова","The mission may end. The evidence remains.":"Миссия может закончиться. Доказательства остаются.","Six NASA explorers: what they left behind, and whether it still works.":"Шесть исследователей NASA: что они оставили после себя и работает ли это до сих пор.","MARS ROVER · ON MARS SINCE 2021":"МАРСОХОД · НА МАРСЕ С 2021 ГОДА","Exploring Jezero Crater, an ancient lake bed, and collecting rock samples for a possible return to Earth. In 2024 it found potential biosignatures in the rock “Cheyava Falls”: intriguing clues, not proof of life.":"Исследует кратер Езеро, дно древнего озера, и собирает образцы пород для возможной доставки на Землю. В 2024 году он нашёл возможные биосигнатуры в камне «Чейава-Фоллс»: интересные зацепки, но не доказательство жизни.","Launched":"Запуск","Where now":"Где сейчас","Jezero Crater rim, Mars":"Край кратера Езеро, Марс","Status":"Статус","Active, to about 2028":"Работает, примерно до 2028 года","Choose a spacecraft":"Выберите аппарат","LEARN MORE":"ПОДРОБНЕЕ","Drag the model to turn it":"Перетащите модель, чтобы повернуть","Image":"Фото","Illustration":"Иллюстрация","3D model:":"3D-модель:","Scroll to the next section":"Перейти к следующему разделу","Missions: sections":"Миссии: разделы","The idea":"Идея","Live now":"Сейчас","What does a spacecraft leave behind?":"Что оставляет после себя космический аппарат?","Six pieces of hardware, from a mirror the size of a suitcase on the Moon to a probe beyond the Sun’s influence. For each one: where it is, why it was built, what it taught us, whether it still works, and where to check. The mission may end. The evidence remains.":"Шесть аппаратов: от зеркала размером с чемодан на Луне до зонда за пределами влияния Солнца. Для каждого: где он, зачем его построили, чему он нас научил, работает ли он сейчас и где это проверить. Миссия может закончиться. Доказательства остаются.","years since Armstrong and Aldrin left the Apollo 11 reflector on the Moon. Observatories still fire lasers at it.":"лет назад Армстронг и Олдрин оставили на Луне отражатель Apollo 11. Обсерватории до сих пор посылают в него лазер.","years since Voyager 1 launched. It is still sending data from interstellar space.":"лет назад стартовал Voyager 1. Он до сих пор присылает данные из межзвёздного пространства.","days Sojourner worked on Mars, against a plan of 7.":"дня проработал Sojourner на Марсе вместо запланированных 7.","years Spirit worked on Mars, on a mission planned for 90 days.":"лет проработал Spirit на Марсе, хотя миссию планировали на 90 дней.","years Opportunity worked on Mars, on a mission planned for 90 days.":"лет проработал Opportunity на Марсе, хотя миссию планировали на 90 дней.","km driven by Perseverance, a record on another world. It is still driving.":"км проехал Perseverance — рекорд на другой планете. И он продолжает ехать.","Where they are, this second":"Где они прямо сейчас","Perseverance’s figures come live from NASA’s mission feed. The Moon and Voyager 1 are calculated every second from JPL data. The silent rovers count the days since their last contact.":"Данные Perseverance приходят в реальном времени из ленты миссии NASA. Луна и Voyager 1 рассчитываются каждую секунду по данным JPL. Для замолчавших марсоходов считаются дни с последней связи.","Exists or works? The four status labels":"Существует или работает? Четыре статуса","Exists or works?":"Существует или работает?","Operating":"Работает","Active and returning science.":"Работает и присылает научные данные.","Passive, still used":"Пассивный, всё ещё используется","No power at all, yet still part of today’s measurements.":"Совсем без питания, но всё ещё участвует в сегодняшних измерениях.","Transmitting, limited":"Передаёт данные, ограниченно","Still sending data, with fewer instruments switched on.":"Всё ещё передаёт данные, но включено меньше приборов.","On surface, not working":"На поверхности, не работает","Still there, no longer operating.":"Всё ещё на месте, но больше не работает.","Apollo 11 laser retroreflector":"Лазерный отражатель Apollo 11","Calculated · JPL data":"Расчёт · данные JPL","Earth–Moon distance now":"Расстояние Земля–Луна сейчас","A laser pulse there and back takes":"Лазерный импульс туда и обратно летит","Since Eagle landed (July 20, 1969, 20:17 UTC)":"С посадки Eagle (20 июля 1969, 20:17 UTC)","Moon distance computed with Meeus’ lunar theory, checked against":"Расстояние до Луны рассчитано по лунной теории Миуса и сверено с","to within 20 km.":"с точностью до 20 км.","See it in 3D":"Посмотреть в 3D","Distance from Earth now":"Расстояние от Земли сейчас","From the Sun":"От Солнца","Its radio signal needs":"Его радиосигналу нужно","Moving away from the Sun at":"Удаляется от Солнца со скоростью","Interpolated from":"Интерполировано по","every second.":"каждую секунду.","Counted from last contact":"Отсчёт от последней связи","Silent for":"Молчит уже","That is about":"Это примерно","Last data from Mars":"Последние данные с Марса","Worked":"Проработал","83 days, against a plan of 7":"83 дня вместо запланированных 7","Last contact":"Последняя связь","Drove":"Проехал","7.73 km on a 90-day mission":"7,73 км за миссию, рассчитанную на 90 дней","45.16 km on a 90-day mission":"45,16 км за миссию, рассчитанную на 90 дней","Live · NASA feed":"В реальном времени · лента NASA","Driven on Mars":"Проехал по Марсу","Latest drive":"Последний выезд","Where it is":"Где он","Mission day now (sol)":"День миссии сейчас (сол)","Live from NASA’s":"В реальном времени из","mission map":"карты миссии","and":"и","raw images":"необработанных снимков","feeds.":"NASA.","· Updated every second. Spirit, Opportunity and Sojourner count from their last contact, not from a known moment of failure.":"· Обновляется каждую секунду. Для Spirit, Opportunity и Sojourner отсчёт идёт от последней связи, а не от известного момента поломки.","The real Solar System, today":"Настоящая Солнечная система сегодня","Where every object is right now, the planets in their true positions for today’s date, and the photographs that prove it.":"Где каждый аппарат прямо сейчас, планеты на своих настоящих местах на сегодняшнюю дату и фотографии, которые это доказывают.","Explore: sections":"Исследовать: разделы","Map":"Карта","Photos":"Фото","Fly the evidence trail":"Пройдите по следу доказательств","Where all six really are today, worked out from NASA and JPL data. Distances are squeezed so the planets fit; Voyager 1, about 170 times farther from the Sun than Earth, sits past a break in the scale. Tap a glowing pin to open that object, or a planet for its key facts.":"Где на самом деле сейчас все шесть, по данным NASA и JPL. Расстояния сжаты, чтобы поместились планеты; Voyager 1, который примерно в 170 раз дальше от Солнца, чем Земля, стоит за разрывом шкалы. Нажмите на светящуюся точку, чтобы открыть аппарат, или на планету, чтобы увидеть её главные факты.","Map of the Solar System for today's date, with the six objects pinned at their real directions from the Sun. Use the buttons under the map to open an object.":"Карта Солнечной системы на сегодня: шесть аппаратов отмечены по их настоящим направлениям от Солнца. Чтобы открыть аппарат, используйте кнопки под картой.","Voyager 1 right now · JPL Horizons":"Voyager 1 прямо сейчас · JPL Horizons","Check NASA’s live figure ↗":"Сверить с живыми данными NASA ↗","Time travel":"Путешествие во времени","Days from today":"Дней от сегодня","Today":"Сегодня","Play":"Запустить","Pause":"Пауза","Close the planet facts":"Закрыть факты о планете","Planet":"Планета","Mean distance from the Sun":"Среднее расстояние от Солнца","One orbit (a year)":"Один оборот (год)","Diameter":"Диаметр","Known moons":"Известные спутники","Visited by our objects":"Кто из наших аппаратов был рядом","From Earth on this date":"От Земли на эту дату","Moon counts are NASA’s as of 2026 (Saturn 293, Jupiter 115 recognised by the IAU, Uranus 29) and keep growing.":"Число спутников — по данным NASA на 2026 год (Сатурн 293, Юпитер 115 признанных МАС, Уран 29), и оно продолжает расти.","Planet positions are calculated for the chosen date from JPL’s orbital elements (accurate to a fraction of a degree). Voyager 1 is interpolated from the JPL Horizons ephemeris, and the Moon’s distance comes from Meeus’ lunar theory. Directions are true; distances are compressed.":"Положения планет рассчитываются на выбранную дату по орбитальным элементам JPL (с точностью до долей градуса). Voyager 1 интерполирован по эфемеридам JPL Horizons, а расстояние до Луны — по лунной теории Миуса. Направления настоящие, расстояния сжаты.","Evidence you can see":"Доказательства, которые можно увидеть","Real photographs from the Moon, Mars and deep space, each with what it proves. Click any picture to enlarge it.":"Настоящие фотографии с Луны, Марса и из дальнего космоса — и что каждая из них доказывает. Нажмите на снимок, чтобы увеличить.","Buzz Aldrin beside the laser reflector he had just set up, July 20, 1969. Proof it is there: observatories still bounce lasers off it today.":"Базз Олдрин рядом с только что установленным лазерным отражателем, 20 июля 1969 года. Доказательство, что он там: обсерватории и сегодня отражают от него лазер.","Eagle, the Lunar Module that carried the reflector to the Moon. Its lower half is still standing at Tranquility Base.":"Eagle — лунный модуль, который доставил отражатель на Луну. Его нижняя часть до сих пор стоит на базе Спокойствия.","Earth from lunar orbit. The Moon always keeps the same face towards us, so the reflector sees Earth in the same part of its sky.":"Земля с лунной орбиты. Луна всегда повёрнута к нам одной стороной, поэтому отражатель видит Землю в одной и той же части неба.","Apollo 15, two years later, left a bigger reflector with 300 prisms. Observatories range to the Apollo arrays together.":"Apollo 15 два года спустя оставил отражатель побольше, на 300 призм. Обсерватории измеряют расстояние до всех отражателей Apollo вместе.","The “Pale Blue Dot”, Feb. 14, 1990: Earth from about 6 billion km. Voyager 1’s cameras were switched off soon after to save power.":"«Бледно-голубая точка», 14 февраля 1990 года: Земля с расстояния около 6 млрд км. Вскоре после этого камеры Voyager 1 выключили, чтобы экономить энергию.","Sojourner pressing its spectrometer against the rock “Yogi”: the first chemical analysis of a rock by a rover on Mars.":"Sojourner прижимает спектрометр к камню «Йоги»: первый химический анализ камня марсоходом на Марсе.","The Pathfinder lander, Sojourner’s only radio link to Earth. When its battery gave out in 1997, the rover went silent too.":"Посадочный модуль Pathfinder — единственная радиосвязь Sojourner с Землёй. Когда в 1997 году его батарея отказала, замолчал и марсоход.","Spirit’s solar panels in 2005, dusty after two years. All its power came from sunlight on this deck, the weakness that ended it.":"Солнечные панели Spirit в 2005 году, запылённые за два года. Вся его энергия шла от солнечного света на этих панелях — это и стало слабым местом.","Opportunity in 2014, after wind had cleaned its panels. Clean panels kept it going for years, until the 2018 dust storm.":"Opportunity в 2014 году, после того как ветер очистил его панели. Чистые панели годами продлевали ему жизнь — до пылевой бури 2018 года.","Perseverance beside “Cheyava Falls”, July 2024: the rock whose potential biosignatures are now being studied.":"Perseverance рядом с «Чейава-Фоллс», июль 2024 года: камень, возможные биосигнатуры которого сейчас изучают.","Rocks in Jezero Crater beside a Perseverance wheel. The crater was once a lake, which is why the rover was sent here.":"Камни в кратере Езеро рядом с колесом Perseverance. Когда-то кратер был озером — поэтому марсоход и отправили сюда.","Perseverance seen from orbit by HiRISE, June 13, 2026: an independent check that it is where NASA says.":"Perseverance, снятый с орбиты камерой HiRISE 13 июня 2026 года: независимая проверка того, что он там, где говорит NASA.","How do we know?":"Откуда мы это знаем?","Fifty-seven years of evidence, every claim with its evidence and its limits, four short films and a test.":"Пятьдесят семь лет доказательств, каждое утверждение с доказательствами и их ограничениями, четыре коротких фильма и тест.","Learn: sections":"Учиться: разделы","Timeline":"Хронология","Evidence lab":"Лаборатория доказательств","Films":"Фильмы","Test yourself":"Проверь себя","Achievements":"Достижения","57 years of evidence":"57 лет доказательств","From the first moonwalk to an off-world driving record, year by year. Each event is marked with the object it belongs to.":"От первой прогулки по Луне до рекорда пробега на другой планете, год за годом. У каждого события отмечен аппарат, к которому оно относится.","Apollo 11 launches from Kennedy Space Center, Florida.":"Apollo 11 стартует из Космического центра Кеннеди во Флориде.","Apollo 11 reflector":"Отражатель Apollo 11","Armstrong and Aldrin land in the Sea of Tranquility and walk on the Moon.":"Армстронг и Олдрин садятся в Море Спокойствия и выходят на Луну.","The reflector is set up near the end of the moonwalk (UTC date).":"Отражатель устанавливают в конце выхода на поверхность (дата по UTC).","Apollo 14 and Apollo 15 leave two more reflector arrays.":"Apollo 14 и Apollo 15 оставляют ещё два отражателя.","Launched from Cape Canaveral, Florida.":"Запущен с мыса Канаверал во Флориде.","Voyager 2 launches, two weeks before Voyager 1.":"Стартует Voyager 2 — за две недели до Voyager 1.","Closest approach to Jupiter.":"Максимальное сближение с Юпитером.","Voyager 1 pictures reveal volcanoes erupting on Io, a moon of Jupiter.":"Снимки Voyager 1 показывают извергающиеся вулканы на Ио, спутнике Юпитера.","Closest approach to Saturn and Titan.":"Максимальное сближение с Сатурном и Титаном.","Takes the “Pale Blue Dot”; cameras are switched off.":"Делает снимок «Бледно-голубая точка»; камеры выключают.","Mars Pathfinder launches from Cape Canaveral, Florida.":"Mars Pathfinder стартует с мыса Канаверал во Флориде.","Lands in Ares Vallis, bouncing on airbags.":"Садится в долине Арес, подпрыгивая на надувных подушках.","Sojourner rolls down a ramp onto Mars.":"Sojourner съезжает по трапу на Марс.","Studies its first rocks, “Barnacle Bill” and “Yogi”.":"Изучает свои первые камни — «Барнакл Билл» и «Йоги».","Last data from the mission.":"Последние данные миссии.","After 35 years, ranging is accurate to about 2 cm.":"Через 35 лет точность измерения расстояния — около 2 см.","Lands in Gusev Crater.":"Садится в кратер Гусев.","Lands in Eagle crater, Meridiani Planum (US time).":"Садится в кратер Eagle на плато Меридиана (по времени США).","Films dust devils in motion.":"Снимает пылевые вихри в движении.","Finds the “Heat Shield Rock” meteorite.":"Находит метеорит «Heat Shield Rock».","Finds nearly pure silica.":"Находит почти чистый кремнезём.","Gets stuck in soft soil.":"Застревает в мягком грунте.","Last contact with Earth.":"Последняя связь с Землёй.","NASA ends the mission.":"NASA завершает миссию.","Reaches Endeavour Crater.":"Добирается до кратера Индевор.","Crosses the heliopause into interstellar space.":"Пересекает гелиопаузу и выходит в межзвёздное пространство.","Drives on a 32° slope, the steepest for any Mars rover.":"Едет по склону в 32° — самому крутому для марсохода.","Last contact, during a planet-wide dust storm.":"Последняя связь — во время глобальной пылевой бури.","After 50 years, measurements reach a few millimetres.":"Через 50 лет точность измерений доходит до нескольких миллиметров.","Lands in Jezero Crater.":"Садится в кратер Езеро.","Collects the “Sapphire Canyon” sample from “Cheyava Falls”.":"Берёт образец «Сапфировый каньон» из камня «Чейава-Фоллс».","Potential biosignatures published in Nature.":"Возможные биосигнатуры опубликованы в журнале Nature.","LECP instrument switched off to save power.":"Прибор LECP выключен ради экономии энергии.","Will be one light-day (about 25.9 billion km) from Earth.":"Будет в одном световом дне (около 25,9 млрд км) от Земли.","Passes a marathon distance (42.2 km).":"Проезжает марафонскую дистанцию (42,2 км).","Sets the off-world driving record.":"Устанавливает рекорд пробега на другой планете.","First extended mission begins.":"Начинается первая расширенная миссия.","Claim, evidence, limits":"Утверждение, доказательства, ограничения","Every claim is labelled: ✓ an established finding, ≈ an interpretation, ? an open question. Open a record to see the evidence, its limits and the source.":"У каждого утверждения есть метка: ✓ установленный факт, ≈ интерпретация, ? открытый вопрос. Откройте запись, чтобы увидеть доказательства, их ограничения и источник.","Object":"Аппарат","All objects":"Все аппараты","Category":"Категория","All categories":"Все категории","Established":"Установлено","Interpretation":"Интерпретация","Unresolved":"Открытый вопрос","✓ Established":"✓ Установлено","≈ Interpretation":"≈ Интерпретация","? Unresolved":"? Открытый вопрос","Laser ranging measures the Earth–Moon distance to within a few millimetres.":"Лазерная локация измеряет расстояние Земля–Луна с точностью до нескольких миллиметров.","Evidence":"Доказательства","Laser pulses fired from observatories and timed on their round trip to the reflector arrays, for more than five decades.":"Лазерные импульсы из обсерваторий и время их полёта до отражателей и обратно — более пятидесяти лет измерений.","Limits":"Ограничения","The returns are extremely faint: in good conditions about one photon every few seconds.":"Отражённый сигнал очень слабый: в хороших условиях — примерно один фотон за несколько секунд.","Source":"Источник","The Moon is moving away from Earth by about 3.8 cm a year.":"Луна удаляется от Земли примерно на 3,8 см в год.","Decades of lunar laser ranging.":"Десятилетия лазерной локации Луны.","A long-term average; models keep refining it.":"Это среднее за долгий срок; модели продолжают его уточнять.","The Moon has a fluid core.":"У Луны жидкое ядро.","Lunar laser ranging data, which showed this about 20 years before 2019.":"Данные лазерной локации Луны, которые показали это примерно за 20 лет до 2019 года.","Indirect: worked out from how the Moon moves, not seen directly.":"Косвенно: выведено из того, как движется Луна, а не увидено напрямую.","Io, a moon of Jupiter, has active volcanoes.":"На Ио, спутнике Юпитера, есть действующие вулканы.","Voyager 1 pictures from March 1979 showing volcanic plumes.":"Снимки Voyager 1 в марте 1979 года с вулканическими выбросами.","A flyby snapshot: later missions are needed to follow how the eruptions change.":"Снимок с пролёта: чтобы следить, как меняются извержения, нужны более поздние миссии.","Voyager 1 left the heliosphere and entered interstellar space on Aug. 25, 2012.":"Voyager 1 покинул гелиосферу и вошёл в межзвёздное пространство 25 августа 2012 года.","Its instruments measured the change from the Sun’s particles to the interstellar medium.":"Его приборы зафиксировали переход от частиц Солнца к межзвёздной среде.","Exactly where the boundary lies was debated at the time.":"Где именно проходит граница, в то время обсуждалось.","A small wheeled rover can drive and do science on Mars.":"Небольшой колёсный марсоход может ездить и вести исследования на Марсе.","Sojourner drove about 100 m and worked 83 days against a 7-day plan.":"Sojourner проехал около 100 м и проработал 83 дня вместо запланированных 7.","One small rover at one landing site, never more than about 12 m from its lander.":"Один маленький марсоход в одном месте посадки, не дальше примерно 12 м от своего посадочного модуля.","Running water once shaped the Ares Vallis landing site.":"Когда-то текущая вода сформировала место посадки в долине Арес.","Rounded pebbles and rocks that look like conglomerates.":"Окатанная галька и камни, похожие на конгломераты.","Based on pictures and a few chemical analyses at a single site.":"Основано на снимках и нескольких химических анализах в одном месте.","The silica-rich soil at Home Plate formed around hot springs or steam vents.":"Богатый кремнезёмом грунт у Home Plate образовался возле горячих источников или паровых выходов.","Spirit’s broken, dragging wheel exposed soil about 90% silica.":"Сломанное колесо Spirit, которое он тащил, вскрыло грунт, примерно на 90% состоящий из кремнезёма.","More than one hot-water setting fits the data; it is read by comparison with places on Earth.":"Данным подходит не один вариант с горячей водой; их толкуют по сравнению с местами на Земле.","Water at the “Comanche” outcrop was not acidic.":"Вода у обнажения «Команчи» не была кислой.","Carbonates about ten times more abundant than in any Martian rock studied before.":"Карбонатов примерно в десять раз больше, чем в любом изученном ранее марсианском камне.","One outcrop; it does not tell how long the water lasted.":"Одно обнажение; оно не говорит, как долго там была вода.","Liquid water once soaked Meridiani Planum.":"Когда-то жидкая вода пропитывала плато Меридиана.","Hematite spherules (“blueberries”) and bright gypsum veins.":"Гематитовые шарики («черника») и светлые прожилки гипса.","That early water was acidic, which is hard on life.":"Та ранняя вода была кислой, а это тяжёлые условия для жизни.","Jezero Crater once held a lake and a river delta.":"Когда-то в кратере Езеро были озеро и речная дельта.","Delta layers imaged and sampled by the rover.":"Слои дельты, снятые и опробованные марсоходом.","How long the lake lasted is still being worked out.":"Сколько существовало озеро, ещё выясняют.","Was there ever microbial life on Mars?":"Была ли когда-нибудь на Марсе микробная жизнь?","The “Sapphire Canyon” sample holds potential biosignatures (Nature, Sept. 2025).":"В образце «Сапфировый каньон» есть возможные биосигнатуры (Nature, сентябрь 2025).","The same minerals can form without life. Confirming it needs labs on Earth, and sample return is not yet approved.":"Те же минералы могут образоваться и без жизни. Для подтверждения нужны лаборатории на Земле, а доставка образцов ещё не одобрена.","Why they went quiet":"Почему они замолчали","Four short films made from NASA photographs, with narration and subtitles: what happened to each spacecraft that lost contact or had to slow down, and why.":"Четыре коротких фильма из фотографий NASA, с озвучкой и субтитрами: что случилось с каждым аппаратом, который потерял связь или был вынужден работать в ограниченном режиме, и почему.","Its lander’s battery failed":"Отказала батарея посадочного модуля","Sojourner: the rover that could not call home":"Sojourner: марсоход, который не смог позвонить домой","Stuck in sand before winter":"Застрял в песке перед зимой","Spirit: stuck before winter":"Spirit: застрял перед зимой","A dust storm hid the Sun":"Пылевая буря закрыла Солнце","Opportunity: the storm that hid the Sun":"Opportunity: буря, закрывшая Солнце","Its power is running out":"У него заканчивается энергия","Voyager 1: running out of power, still talking":"Voyager 1: энергия на исходе, но он ещё на связи","How much do you know?":"Сколько ты знаешь?","Three rounds: is it still working, the six missions, and the words of space exploration. Questions change every time you play.":"Три раунда: работает ли он ещё, шесть миссий и слова космических исследований. Вопросы меняются в каждой игре.","Three rounds. Every answer comes with the reason, and good scores unlock achievements.":"Три раунда. К каждому ответу есть объяснение, а хорошие результаты открывают достижения.","Working or existing?":"Работает или просто существует?","6 questions: which status label fits each object today":"6 вопросов: какой статус подходит каждому аппарату сегодня","Not played yet":"Ещё не играли","Missions round":"Раунд о миссиях","10 questions about the six objects":"10 вопросов о шести аппаратах","Glossary round":"Раунд по словарю","8 questions: match the word to its meaning":"8 вопросов: подберите слово к значению","Your mission log":"Твой бортовой журнал","Six achievements for what you learn: the six objects, the films, the three test rounds and the glossary. Progress is saved in this browser only.":"Шесть достижений за то, что ты узнаёшь: шесть аппаратов, фильмы, три раунда теста и словарь. Прогресс сохраняется только в этом браузере.","Grand tour":"Большое путешествие","Open the details of all six objects.":"Открой подробности всех шести аппаратов.","Score 6 out of 6 in the status round.":"Набери 6 из 6 в раунде о статусах.","Locked":"Закрыто","Mission specialist":"Специалист миссии","Score 9 or 10 in the missions round.":"Набери 9 или 10 в раунде о миссиях.","Word wizard":"Знаток слов","Score 8 out of 8 in the glossary round.":"Набери 8 из 8 в раунде по словарю.","Dictionary diver":"Исследователь словаря","Open 10 different glossary terms.":"Открой 10 разных терминов словаря.","Film buff":"Киноман","Watch all four films to the end.":"Посмотри все четыре фильма до конца.","Side by side, with sources":"Рядом, с источниками","All six objects in one table, how the facts were checked, and every NASA page we used.":"Все шесть аппаратов в одной таблице, как проверялись факты и все страницы NASA, которые мы использовали.","Compare: sections":"Сравнить: разделы","Method":"Метод","Six objects side by side":"Шесть аппаратов рядом","One row per spacecraft: when it left, where it is and whether it works. The full story of each is one click away.":"По строке на аппарат: когда стартовал, где находится и работает ли. Полная история каждого — в один клик.","Spacecraft":"Аппарат","Status today":"Статус сегодня","Sources":"Источники","Sea of Tranquility, Moon":"Море Спокойствия, Луна","It has no power and no moving parts, which is why it has lasted more than 55 years.":"У него нет ни питания, ни движущихся частей — поэтому он работает уже больше 55 лет.","Interstellar space":"Межзвёздное пространство","Two instruments are still on: the magnetometer (MAG) and the plasma wave subsystem (PWS).":"Включены ещё два прибора: магнитометр (MAG) и прибор для изучения плазменных волн (PWS).","Ares Vallis, Mars":"Долина Арес, Марс","It never went more than about 12 m from the lander, because it talked to Earth through the lander’s radio.":"Он никогда не отъезжал от посадочного модуля дальше примерно 12 м, потому что связывался с Землёй через его радио.","Gusev Crater, Mars":"Кратер Гусев, Марс","Got stuck in soft soil on May 1, 2009.":"Застрял в мягком грунте 1 мая 2009 года.","Endeavour Crater, Mars":"Кратер Индевор, Марс","In 2018 a dust storm covered the whole planet and blocked sunlight from its solar panels.":"В 2018 году пылевая буря накрыла всю планету и закрыла солнечный свет от его солнечных панелей.","Its driving systems are fully working.":"Его ходовые системы полностью исправны.","Still there is not the same as still working":"Всё ещё там — не то же самое, что всё ещё работает","Spirit and Opportunity are still on Mars, but they have been silent for years. Voyager 1 still works and sends data, but with only two of its ten instruments switched on.":"Spirit и Opportunity всё ещё на Марсе, но молчат уже много лет. Voyager 1 всё ещё работает и присылает данные, но включены только два из десяти его приборов.","How the evidence stays honest":"Как доказательства остаются честными","Label every claim":"Помечать каждое утверждение","Established, interpretation or open question. Never blended together.":"Установленный факт, интерпретация или открытый вопрос. Никогда не смешиваются.","Exists is not works":"Существует — не значит работает","Every object carries a status, because hardware stays long after it stops.":"У каждого аппарата есть статус, потому что техника остаётся надолго после того, как перестаёт работать.","NASA first":"Сначала NASA","Each object links at least two primary sources. Figures that change are sent to the live NASA page.":"У каждого аппарата есть ссылки минимум на два первичных источника. За меняющимися цифрами мы отправляем на живую страницу NASA.","Nothing invented":"Ничего не выдумано","No simulated telemetry, no made-up discoveries. Simplified 3D models and estimates are marked as such.":"Никакой имитации телеметрии, никаких выдуманных открытий. Упрощённые 3D-модели и оценки помечены.","About":"О проекте","About Singularity’s":"О Singularity’s","A student project about what NASA’s explorers leave behind, and how we know whether they still work.":"Школьный проект о том, что оставляют после себя исследователи NASA и как мы узнаём, работают ли они ещё.","Why":"Зачем","Space missions end, but the hardware and the evidence stay. Singularity’s shows what six NASA explorers left behind and whether each one still works.":"Космические миссии заканчиваются, но техника и доказательства остаются. Singularity’s показывает, что оставили после себя шесть исследователей NASA и работает ли каждый из них.","For whom":"Для кого","School students who want to understand how we know what we know about the Moon, Mars and deep space.":"Для школьников, которые хотят понять, откуда мы знаем то, что знаем о Луне, Марсе и дальнем космосе.","Where the data comes from":"Откуда данные","NASA and JPL mission pages, NASA’s 3D models and photographs, the JPL Horizons ephemeris and NASA’s live Perseverance feeds. Every claim links to its source.":"Страницы миссий NASA и JPL, 3D-модели и фотографии NASA, эфемериды JPL Horizons и живые ленты Perseverance от NASA. У каждого утверждения есть ссылка на источник.","How the facts were checked":"Как проверялись факты","The team’s analyst collected the facts into one table on Oct. 22, 2026, from NASA pages only. Calculated figures are labelled as calculated, and the simplified 3D models as simplified.":"Аналитик команды собрал факты в одну таблицу 22 октября 2026 года — только со страниц NASA. Рассчитанные цифры помечены как расчётные, а упрощённые 3D-модели — как упрощённые.","The team":"Команда","Team lead: Muzayana. Analyst, engineer and programmer: the team of four.":"Руководитель команды: Музаяна. Аналитик, инженер и программист — команда из четырёх человек.","The words of space exploration":"Слова космических исследований","Every special term used on Singularity’s, explained simply. Underlined words anywhere on the site open these explanations too.":"Все специальные термины Singularity’s простыми словами. Подчёркнутые слова на любой странице тоже открывают эти объяснения.","Filter terms":"Фильтр терминов","Filter terms…":"Найти термин…","Jump to a letter":"Перейти к букве","Alpha Particle X-ray Spectrometer. Pressed against a rock, it measures which chemical elements the rock contains.":"Альфа-рентгеновский спектрометр. Его прижимают к камню, и он измеряет, из каких химических элементов тот состоит.","On Singularity’s:":"На Singularity’s:","Astronomical unit (AU)":"Астрономическая единица (а. е.)","The average distance between Earth and the Sun, about 149.6 million km. Mars orbits about 1.5 AU from the Sun; Voyager 1 is more than 170 AU away.":"Среднее расстояние между Землёй и Солнцем — около 149,6 млн км. Марс обращается примерно в 1,5 а. е. от Солнца; Voyager 1 находится дальше 170 а. е.","Biosignature":"Биосигнатура","A pattern that life could have made. A potential biosignature, like the one in the rock “Cheyava Falls”, is a clue that needs more study, not proof of life.":"След, который могла оставить жизнь. Возможная биосигнатура, как в камне «Чейава-Фоллс», — это зацепка, требующая изучения, а не доказательство жизни.","Deep Space Network":"Сеть дальней космической связи","NASA’s giant radio dishes in California, Spain and Australia. Spread around the globe, they can always reach a distant spacecraft as Earth turns.":"Гигантские антенны NASA в Калифорнии, Испании и Австралии. Они разнесены по всему миру, поэтому, пока Земля вращается, всегда могут связаться с далёким аппаратом.","Ecliptic":"Эклиптика","The flat plane of Earth’s orbit around the Sun. The planets all orbit close to it; Voyager 1 flies about 35° above it.":"Плоскость орбиты Земли вокруг Солнца. Все планеты обращаются близко к ней; Voyager 1 летит примерно на 35° выше неё.","Ephemeris":"Эфемериды","A table of where a planet, moon or spacecraft is at given times. Singularity’s uses the JPL Horizons ephemeris for Voyager 1.":"Таблица положений планеты, спутника или аппарата в заданные моменты времени. Для Voyager 1 Singularity’s использует эфемериды JPL Horizons.","Global dust storm":"Глобальная пылевая буря","A Martian storm that can grow until it wraps the whole planet for weeks and blocks most of the sunlight. The 2018 storm ended Opportunity’s mission.":"Марсианская буря, которая может разрастись так, что на недели окутывает всю планету и закрывает большую часть солнечного света. Буря 2018 года завершила миссию Opportunity.","Golden Record":"Золотая пластинка","A gold-plated copper disc on each Voyager with sounds, music and pictures from Earth, a message for anyone who might find it.":"Позолоченный медный диск на каждом Voyager со звуками, музыкой и изображениями Земли — послание тому, кто может его найти.","Gravity assist":"Гравитационный манёвр","Flying close to a planet to borrow some of its speed. Voyager 1 used Jupiter and Saturn to speed up and change direction.":"Пролёт рядом с планетой, чтобы «одолжить» часть её скорости. Voyager 1 использовал Юпитер и Сатурн, чтобы разогнаться и сменить направление.","Gusev Crater":"Кратер Гусев","A crater about 160 km wide where Spirit landed in January 2004.":"Кратер шириной около 160 км, куда Spirit сел в январе 2004 года.","Hazcam":"Хазкам","Hazard-avoidance cameras mounted low on a rover that watch for rocks and holes near the wheels.":"Камеры для объезда препятствий, установленные низко на марсоходе: они следят за камнями и ямами у колёс.","Heliosphere":"Гелиосфера","The huge bubble that the solar wind, the stream of particles from the Sun, blows around the Solar System. Voyager 1 crossed its edge in 2012.":"Огромный пузырь, который солнечный ветер — поток частиц от Солнца — надувает вокруг Солнечной системы. Voyager 1 пересёк его границу в 2012 году.","Hematite":"Гематит","An iron-oxide mineral. Opportunity found tiny hematite spheres, nicknamed “blueberries”, that formed in water.":"Минерал, оксид железа. Opportunity нашёл крошечные гематитовые шарики, прозванные «черникой», которые образовались в воде.","High-gain antenna":"Остронаправленная антенна","A dish that sends a narrow, strong radio beam. It has to point very precisely at Earth.":"Тарелка, которая посылает узкий мощный радиолуч. Её нужно очень точно направлять на Землю.","The space between the stars, outside the Sun’s heliosphere. Voyager 1 was the first human-made object to reach it.":"Пространство между звёздами, за пределами гелиосферы Солнца. Voyager 1 стал первым рукотворным объектом, который туда добрался.","Jezero Crater":"Кратер Езеро","A 45 km crater on Mars that once held a lake fed by a river. Perseverance explores its old river delta and its rim.":"45-километровый кратер на Марсе, в котором когда-то было озеро, питаемое рекой. Perseverance исследует его древнюю дельту и край.","Lander":"Посадочный модуль","A spacecraft that lands and stays in one place. Sojourner’s lander, Mars Pathfinder, carried the only radio that could reach Earth.":"Аппарат, который садится и остаётся на одном месте. Посадочный модуль Sojourner, Mars Pathfinder, нёс единственное радио, способное достать до Земли.","Light-time":"Время прохождения света","How long light or a radio signal takes to travel a distance, at about 300,000 km every second. From the Moon it takes about 1.3 s; from Voyager 1 almost a whole day. A light-day is about 25.9 billion km.":"Сколько времени свету или радиосигналу нужно, чтобы пройти расстояние, при скорости около 300 000 км в секунду. От Луны — около 1,3 с, от Voyager 1 — почти сутки. Световой день — около 25,9 млрд км.","Lunar laser ranging":"Лазерная локация Луны","Firing laser pulses at the reflectors on the Moon and timing the echo. It measures the Earth–Moon distance to a few millimetres and shows the Moon drifting away by about 3.8 cm a year.":"Посылка лазерных импульсов к отражателям на Луне и измерение времени отражения. Так расстояние Земля–Луна измеряют с точностью до нескольких миллиметров и видят, что Луна удаляется примерно на 3,8 см в год.","Magnetometer":"Магнитометр","An instrument that measures magnetic fields. Voyager 1’s sits on a 13 m boom so the spacecraft’s own magnetism does not disturb it.":"Прибор, измеряющий магнитные поля. У Voyager 1 он стоит на 13-метровой штанге, чтобы ему не мешал магнетизм самого аппарата.","Meridiani Planum":"Плато Меридиана","A flat plain near the Martian equator where Opportunity landed in January 2004.":"Плоская равнина у марсианского экватора, куда Opportunity сел в январе 2004 года.","An experiment on Perseverance that made oxygen from the carbon dioxide in Mars’ thin air, a test for future astronauts.":"Эксперимент на Perseverance, который получал кислород из углекислого газа разреженной атмосферы Марса, — проба для будущих астронавтов.","Orbiter":"Орбитальный аппарат","A spacecraft that circles a planet. Orbiters around Mars relay most rover data to Earth, because they have bigger radios and see Earth more often.":"Аппарат, который вращается вокруг планеты. Орбитальные аппараты у Марса передают на Землю большую часть данных марсоходов: у них мощнее радио и они чаще видят Землю.","Pale Blue Dot":"Бледно-голубая точка","The photo of Earth Voyager 1 took on Feb. 14, 1990 from about 6 billion km away: Earth is less than a single pixel in a sunbeam.":"Снимок Земли, который Voyager 1 сделал 14 февраля 1990 года с расстояния около 6 млрд км: Земля меньше одного пикселя в солнечном луче.","Prime mission":"Основная миссия","How long a mission is first designed and paid for. Spirit and Opportunity were planned for 90 sols; both lasted years longer.":"На какой срок миссию изначально проектируют и финансируют. Spirit и Opportunity планировали на 90 солов; оба проработали на годы дольше.","Retroreflector":"Уголковый отражатель","A device that sends light straight back to where it came from, whatever the angle. The Apollo 11 array has 100 corner-cube prisms of fused silica.":"Устройство, которое возвращает свет точно туда, откуда он пришёл, под любым углом. В отражателе Apollo 11 100 уголковых призм из плавленого кварца.","Rocker-bogie":"Подвеска «рокер-боги»","A six-wheel suspension that lets a rover climb over rocks while keeping every wheel on the ground. Sojourner was the first to use it on Mars.":"Шестиколёсная подвеска, которая позволяет марсоходу переезжать камни, не отрывая ни одного колеса от земли. Sojourner первым использовал её на Марсе.","Rover":"Марсоход (ровер)","A robot vehicle that drives across the surface of another world. All four Mars objects on this site are rovers.":"Робот-вездеход, который ездит по поверхности другой планеты. Все четыре марсианских аппарата на этом сайте — марсоходы.","RTG (nuclear power source)":"РИТЭГ (ядерный источник питания)","A radioisotope thermoelectric generator turns the heat of decaying plutonium-238 into electricity, day and night, with no moving parts. Voyager 1’s RTGs lose about 4 watts a year.":"Радиоизотопный термоэлектрический генератор превращает тепло распада плутония-238 в электричество — днём и ночью, без движущихся частей. РИТЭГи Voyager 1 теряют около 4 ватт в год.","Sample tube":"Пробирка для образца","Perseverance drills rock cores and seals them in tubes. Bringing some of them to Earth has been studied, but how and when is still being decided.":"Perseverance высверливает керны породы и запечатывает их в пробирки. Доставку части из них на Землю изучали, но как и когда это сделать, ещё решают.","Silica":"Кремнезём","Silicon dioxide, the stuff of quartz and glass. The nearly pure silica Spirit dug up forms around hot springs or steam vents, places where life thrives on Earth.":"Диоксид кремния — вещество кварца и стекла. Почти чистый кремнезём, который откопал Spirit, образуется у горячих источников и паровых выходов — там, где на Земле процветает жизнь.","Sol":"Сол","A day on Mars: 24 hours, 39 minutes and 35 seconds. Rover teams count mission days in sols, starting with sol 0 on landing day.":"Сутки на Марсе: 24 часа 39 минут 35 секунд. Команды марсоходов считают дни миссии в солах, начиная с сола 0 в день посадки.","Solar panel":"Солнечная панель","A panel that turns sunlight into electricity. Dust and the weak winter Sun ended the solar-powered Spirit and Opportunity.":"Панель, превращающая солнечный свет в электричество. Пыль и слабое зимнее Солнце погубили Spirit и Opportunity, работавших на солнечной энергии.","Solar wind":"Солнечный ветер","A constant stream of charged particles flowing out from the Sun at hundreds of kilometres per second.":"Постоянный поток заряженных частиц, вылетающих из Солнца со скоростью сотни километров в секунду.","Spectrometer":"Спектрометр","An instrument that splits light or other radiation into its parts to work out what a rock or a gas is made of.":"Прибор, который раскладывает свет или другое излучение на составляющие, чтобы понять, из чего состоит камень или газ.","Telemetry":"Телеметрия","The data a spacecraft sends home about itself and its measurements: temperatures, power, position and science readings.":"Данные, которые аппарат отправляет домой о себе и своих измерениях: температура, питание, положение и научные показания.","Team Singularity’s":"Команда Singularity’s","· Team lead: Muzayana · Analyst · Engineer · Programmer ·":"· Руководитель: Музаяна · Аналитик · Инженер · Программист ·","Team lead: Muzayana":"Руководитель: Музаяна","Analyst":"Аналитик","Engineer":"Инженер","Programmer":"Программист","About the project":"О проекте","Presentation mode":"Режим презентации","Singularity’s · team prototype, October 2026. Facts checked against NASA sources on Oct. 22, 2026. Images, 3D models and data: NASA/JPL-Caltech, NASA VTAD.":"Singularity’s · прототип команды, октябрь 2026. Факты сверены с источниками NASA 22 октября 2026 года. Изображения, 3D-модели и данные: NASA/JPL-Caltech, NASA VTAD.","Singularity’s is an independent student project, not affiliated with or endorsed by NASA. Status and figures change, so confirm them at the linked sources.":"Singularity’s — независимый школьный проект, не связанный с NASA и не одобренный им. Статусы и цифры меняются, поэтому сверяйте их по ссылкам на источники.","Back to top ↑":"Наверх ↑","Enlarged photo":"Увеличенное фото","Close":"Закрыть","Sound":"Звук","Off by default. Space ambience, shooting stars and button clicks.":"По умолчанию выключен. Космический фон, падающие звёзды и щелчки кнопок.","Background ambience":"Фоновый звук","The deep space hum and shooting stars":"Гул дальнего космоса и падающие звёзды","Button sounds":"Звуки кнопок","Clicks, answers and achievements":"Щелчки, ответы и достижения","Film narration":"Озвучка фильмов","Read the films aloud with your browser’s voice":"Читать фильмы вслух голосом браузера","Picture quality":"Качество изображения","3D models":"3D-модели","NASA’s 3D models you can turn and point at. Best on newer devices.":"3D-модели NASA, которые можно вращать и рассматривать по частям. Лучше всего на новых устройствах.","2D photos":"2D-фото","NASA photos instead of 3D. Loads fast and runs smoothly on any device.":"Фото NASA вместо 3D. Быстро загружается и плавно работает на любом устройстве.","Animation":"Анимация","Full":"Полная","Shooting stars and entrance effects.":"Падающие звёзды и эффекты появления.","Reduced":"Уменьшенная","No moving effects: calmer and lighter for slow devices.":"Без движущихся эффектов: спокойнее и легче для медленных устройств.","Reload to apply":"Перезагрузить, чтобы применить","Reset achievements":"Сбросить достижения","Presentation mode (P)":"Режим презентации (P)","Search Singularity’s":"Поиск по Singularity’s","Search spacecraft, facts, words…":"Ищите аппараты, факты, слова…","Search":"Поиск","Close search":"Закрыть поиск","Keywords":"Ключевые слова","Moon":"Луна","laser":"лазер","retroreflector":"отражатель","passive":"пассивный","Earth–Moon distance":"расстояние Земля–Луна","interstellar":"межзвёздное","nuclear power":"ядерная энергия","Jupiter":"Юпитер","Saturn":"Сатурн","heliosphere":"гелиосфера","deep space":"дальний космос","Mars":"Марс","rover":"марсоход","lander":"посадочный модуль","first rover":"первый марсоход","solar power":"солнечная энергия","silica":"кремнезём","stuck in sand":"застрял в песке","winter":"зима","dust storm":"пылевая буря","hematite":"гематит","record drive":"рекорд пробега","samples":"образцы","biosignature":"биосигнатура","active":"работает","Results":"Результаты","Nothing found. Try another word, or a keyword such as #Mars.":"Ничего не найдено. Попробуйте другое слово или ключевое слово, например #Mars.","↑ ↓ to move":"↑ ↓ — перемещение","Enter to open":"Enter — открыть","Ctrl K or / to search from anywhere":"Ctrl K или / — поиск с любой страницы","Close film":"Закрыть фильм","Animated film. The narration is shown as subtitles below the picture.":"Фильм. Озвучка показана субтитрами под изображением.","Play film":"Смотреть фильм","Watch again":"Смотреть снова","Position in the film":"Позиция в фильме","Narration on":"Озвучка включена","Narration off":"Озвучка выключена","Close presentation":"Закрыть презентацию","← Back":"← Назад","Next →":"Далее →","Buzz Aldrin on the Moon beside the seismometer and the laser reflector, with the flag and the Lunar Module behind":"Базз Олдрин на Луне рядом с сейсмометром и лазерным отражателем, за ним флаг и лунный модуль","LASER REFLECTOR · ON THE MOON SINCE 1969":"ЛАЗЕРНЫЙ ОТРАЖАТЕЛЬ · НА ЛУНЕ С 1969 ГОДА","A panel of 100 glass corner cubes that Neil Armstrong and Buzz Aldrin left on the Moon. It needs no power, and observatories still fire lasers at it to time the Earth–Moon distance to within a few millimetres.":"Панель из 100 стеклянных уголковых призм, которую Нил Армстронг и Базз Олдрин оставили на Луне. Ей не нужно питание, и обсерватории до сих пор посылают в неё лазер, чтобы измерять расстояние Земля–Луна с точностью до нескольких миллиметров.","glass corner cubes":"стеклянных уголковых призм","the Moon moves away each year":"на столько Луна удаляется каждый год","power it needs":"энергии ему нужно","55+ years":"55+ лет","still in use":"и всё ещё используется","Built to":"Создан, чтобы","Send laser pulses from Earth straight back to where they came from, so observatories can time the round trip and measure the distance to the Moon.":"Возвращать лазерные импульсы с Земли точно туда, откуда они пришли, чтобы обсерватории могли засечь время полёта туда и обратно и измерить расстояние до Луны.","What it found":"Что он открыл","The Moon is moving away from Earth by about 3.8 cm (1.5 in) a year.":"Луна удаляется от Земли примерно на 3,8 см в год.","The Moon has a fluid core, although scientists had expected a cool, solid one.":"У Луны жидкое ядро, хотя учёные ожидали холодное и твёрдое.","Gravity passes a test of Einstein’s ideas: the Sun pulls on Earth and the Moon in the same way, even though Earth contains more iron.":"Гравитация проходит проверку идей Эйнштейна: Солнце притягивает Землю и Луну одинаково, хотя в Земле больше железа.","The Earth–Moon distance is now measured to within a few millimetres.":"Расстояние Земля–Луна сейчас измеряют с точностью до нескольких миллиметров.","Four telescopes, in New Mexico, France, Italy and Germany, fire lasers at the Apollo arrays.":"Четыре телескопа — в Нью-Мексико, Франции, Италии и Германии — посылают лазер в отражатели Apollo.","Limits: the reflector is far too small to see from Earth, and by the time the laser reaches the Moon the beam is several kilometres wide.":"Ограничения: отражатель слишком мал, чтобы увидеть его с Земли, а к моменту, когда лазер долетает до Луны, луч расширяется до нескольких километров.","The light that comes back is extremely faint: in good conditions about one photon every few seconds, so only a few observatories can do this.":"Возвращающийся свет очень слабый: в хороших условиях — примерно один фотон за несколько секунд, поэтому это умеют лишь немногие обсерватории.","The Apollo 11 Lunar Module standing on the grey lunar surface, with the Sun behind it":"Лунный модуль Apollo 11 на серой лунной поверхности, за ним Солнце","The Lunar Module Eagle on the Sea of Tranquility. The reflector was set up a short walk away.":"Лунный модуль Eagle в Море Спокойствия. Отражатель установили в нескольких шагах от него.","Parts you can point at":"Детали, на которые можно навести","Move the mouse over the 3D model, or tap it, to see these on the spacecraft. This model is a simplified Singularity’s build from NASA dimensions.":"Наведите мышь на 3D-модель или коснитесь её, чтобы увидеть эти детали на аппарате. Это упрощённая модель Singularity’s по размерам NASA.","Move the mouse over the 3D model, or tap it, to see these on the spacecraft.":"Наведите мышь на 3D-модель или коснитесь её, чтобы увидеть эти детали на аппарате.","Corner-cube array":"Блок уголковых призм","100 fused-silica prisms, each 3.8 cm across. Each one sends light straight back to where it came from.":"100 призм из плавленого кварца, каждая 3,8 см в поперечнике. Каждая возвращает свет точно туда, откуда он пришёл.","Aluminium panel":"Алюминиевая панель","46 × 46 cm, tilted toward Earth, which hangs high in the sky above Tranquility Base.":"46 × 46 см, наклонена к Земле, которая висит высоко в небе над базой Спокойствия.","Pallet and legs":"Основание и опоры","Carried out of the Lunar Module and set down by Buzz Aldrin in July 1969. No power, no moving parts, nothing to wear out.":"Вынесен из лунного модуля и установлен Баззом Олдрином в июле 1969 года. Без питания, без движущихся частей — изнашиваться нечему.","Laser pulse from Earth":"Лазерный импульс с Земли","Observatories fire short laser pulses at the array. The round trip takes about 2.5 seconds and only a few photons come back.":"Обсерватории посылают в отражатель короткие лазерные импульсы. Путь туда и обратно занимает около 2,5 секунды, и возвращаются лишь несколько фотонов.","Other spacecraft":"Другие аппараты","simplified model built by Singularity’s from NASA dimensions (not an official NASA model)":"упрощённая модель Singularity’s по размерам NASA (не официальная модель NASA)","Illustration of the Voyager 1 spacecraft with its large dish antenna, entering interstellar space":"Иллюстрация: аппарат Voyager 1 с большой антенной-тарелкой входит в межзвёздное пространство","SPACE PROBE · IN FLIGHT SINCE 1977":"КОСМИЧЕСКИЙ ЗОНД · В ПОЛЁТЕ С 1977 ГОДА","After flying past Jupiter and Saturn, it became the first spacecraft to leave the heliosphere, in 2012. It is still sending data from interstellar space, though only two of its ten instruments remain on.":"Пролетев мимо Юпитера и Сатурна, в 2012 году он первым из аппаратов покинул гелиосферу. Он до сих пор присылает данные из межзвёздного пространства, хотя включены только два из его десяти приборов.","Watch: why it is limited":"Смотреть: почему он ограничен","Watch: why it went silent":"Смотреть: почему он замолчал","launched":"запуск","instruments still on":"приборов ещё включены","power lost every year":"мощности теряется каждый год","1 light-day":"1 световой день","away from Earth on Nov. 18, 2026 (expected)":"от Земли 18 ноября 2026 года (ожидается)","Fly past Jupiter and Saturn and study the two giant planets, their rings and their moons, including Saturn’s largest moon, Titan.":"Пролететь мимо Юпитера и Сатурна и изучить две планеты-гиганта, их кольца и спутники, включая крупнейший спутник Сатурна — Титан.","Jupiter has a faint ring, and two moons nobody knew about: Thebe and Metis.":"У Юпитера есть слабое кольцо и два неизвестных ранее спутника: Фива и Метида.","Its pictures from March 1979 showed volcanoes erupting on Io, a moon of Jupiter: the first active volcanoes seen beyond Earth.":"Его снимки в марте 1979 года показали извергающиеся вулканы на Ио, спутнике Юпитера, — первые действующие вулканы, увиденные за пределами Земли.","Saturn has five more moons, a new ring, and small “shepherd” moons that keep some rings sharp.":"У Сатурна нашлись ещё пять спутников, новое кольцо и маленькие спутники-«пастухи», которые сохраняют чёткость некоторых колец.","Titan’s atmosphere is about 90% nitrogen and so thick it hides the surface completely.":"Атмосфера Титана примерно на 90% состоит из азота и настолько плотная, что полностью скрывает поверхность.","It is the first spacecraft to leave the heliosphere, the bubble of the Sun’s influence, so it measures interstellar space directly.":"Это первый аппарат, покинувший гелиосферу — пузырь влияния Солнца, поэтому он измеряет межзвёздное пространство напрямую.","On Feb. 14, 1990 it took the “Pale Blue Dot”: Earth seen from about 6 billion km away.":"14 февраля 1990 года он сделал снимок «Бледно-голубая точка»: Земля с расстояния около 6 млрд км.","The low-energy charged particles instrument (LECP) was switched off on Apr. 17, 2026 to save power.":"Прибор для изучения заряженных частиц низкой энергии (LECP) выключили 17 апреля 2026 года, чтобы сэкономить энергию.","Its nuclear power sources (RTGs) lose about 4 W every year, so the team switches instruments off one by one.":"Его ядерные источники питания (РИТЭГи) теряют около 4 Вт каждый год, поэтому команда выключает приборы один за другим.","The cameras have been off since 1990: no new pictures, only measurements.":"Камеры выключены с 1990 года: новых снимков нет, только измерения.","A radio signal now takes almost a full day to reach Earth.":"Радиосигнал теперь идёт до Земли почти целые сутки.","Earth as a single faint bright dot inside a band of scattered sunlight against black space":"Земля — одна слабая светлая точка в полосе рассеянного солнечного света на фоне чёрного космоса","“Pale Blue Dot Revisited”: Earth (the tiny dot in the light band) from about 6 billion km. Colours are false.":"«Бледно-голубая точка» в новой обработке: Земля (крошечная точка в световой полосе) с расстояния около 6 млрд км. Цвета условные.","A 3.7 m dish kept pointed at Earth. Its signal now takes almost a day to arrive.":"3,7-метровая тарелка, всегда направленная на Землю. Её сигнал теперь идёт почти сутки.","Ten-sided body":"Десятигранный корпус","Holds the computers and radios. Bolted to the outside is the Golden Record of sounds and pictures from Earth.":"Внутри компьютеры и радиоаппаратура. Снаружи прикреплена Золотая пластинка со звуками и изображениями Земли.","Magnetometer boom":"Штанга магнитометра","A 13 m boom keeps the magnetometer away from the spacecraft’s own magnetism. MAG is one of the two instruments still on.":"13-метровая штанга уносит магнитометр подальше от собственного магнетизма аппарата. MAG — один из двух ещё включённых приборов.","Nuclear power sources (RTGs)":"Ядерные источники питания (РИТЭГи)","Three plutonium generators on their own boom. They lose about 4 W a year, so instruments are switched off one by one.":"Три плутониевых генератора на отдельной штанге. Они теряют около 4 Вт в год, поэтому приборы выключают один за другим.","Science boom":"Научная штанга","Carried the cameras, switched off for good in 1990 after the Pale Blue Dot.":"Несла камеры, которые навсегда выключили в 1990 году после «Бледно-голубой точки».","Active, 2 of 10 instruments on":"Работает, включены 2 прибора из 10","The small Sojourner rover pressing its spectrometer against a large rock called Yogi":"Маленький марсоход Sojourner прижимает спектрометр к большому камню «Йоги»","MARS ROVER · WORKED 1997":"МАРСОХОД · РАБОТАЛ В 1997 ГОДУ","The first wheeled vehicle on another planet, about the size of a microwave oven. Planned for 7 days, it worked for 83, analysed the rocks around the Pathfinder lander and found signs that water once flowed there.":"Первая колёсная машина на другой планете, размером примерно с микроволновку. Её рассчитывали на 7 дней, а она проработала 83, изучила камни вокруг модуля Pathfinder и нашла признаки того, что там когда-то текла вода.","rover mass":"масса марсохода","worked, against 7 planned":"работы вместо 7 запланированных","driven in total":"пройдено всего","pictures it took":"снимков сделано","Show that a small wheeled rover can drive and do science on Mars, and that a low-cost landing on airbags works. Its spectrometer (APXS) measured what the nearby rocks and soil were made of.":"Доказать, что маленький колёсный марсоход может ездить и вести исследования на Марсе и что недорогая посадка на надувных подушках работает. Его спектрометр (APXS) измерил, из чего состоят ближайшие камни и грунт.","It became the first wheeled vehicle on another planet.":"Он стал первой колёсной машиной на другой планете.","Rounded pebbles and rocks that look like conglomerates: running water once shaped the landing site, so ancient Mars was warmer and wetter.":"Окатанная галька и камни, похожие на конгломераты: место посадки когда-то сформировала текущая вода, значит, древний Марс был теплее и влажнее.","Dust in the Martian air is magnetic, probably because of a mineral called maghemite.":"Пыль в марсианском воздухе магнитная — вероятно, из-за минерала маггемита.","The mission watched dust devils and early-morning clouds of water ice.":"Миссия наблюдала пылевые вихри и утренние облака из водяного льда.","Its airbag landing was later used for Spirit and Opportunity.":"Посадку на надувных подушках позже использовали для Spirit и Opportunity.","The last data came on Sept. 27, 1997, when contact with the lander was lost.":"Последние данные пришли 27 сентября 1997 года, когда пропала связь с посадочным модулем.","It lasted 12 times longer than planned.":"Он проработал в 12 раз дольше запланированного.","The rover is still physically on Mars, in Ares Vallis.":"Марсоход до сих пор находится на Марсе, в долине Арес.","The Mars Pathfinder lander seen from above on orange Martian ground, its three solar petals open among deflated airbags":"Посадочный модуль Mars Pathfinder сверху на оранжевом марсианском грунте, три его солнечных лепестка раскрыты среди сдувшихся подушек","The Mars Pathfinder lander on Mars, its petals open among the deflated airbags. Sojourner drove off it down a ramp.":"Посадочный модуль Mars Pathfinder на Марсе, его лепестки раскрыты среди сдувшихся подушек. Sojourner съехал с него по трапу.","Its main power came from 0.2 m² of solar cells on the roof.":"Основную энергию давали 0,2 м² солнечных элементов на крыше.","Front cameras":"Передние камеры","A stereo pair, with laser stripes to judge how tall the rocks ahead were.":"Стереопара с лазерными полосками, чтобы оценивать высоту камней впереди.","Six 13 cm wheels":"Шесть колёс по 13 см","On a rocker-bogie suspension, the idea later used by Spirit, Opportunity and Perseverance.":"На подвеске «рокер-боги» — идею позже использовали Spirit, Opportunity и Perseverance.","APXS spectrometer":"Спектрометр APXS","Pressed against rocks such as “Yogi” to measure which chemical elements they contain.":"Его прижимали к камням вроде «Йоги», чтобы измерить, какие химические элементы в них есть.","Radio antenna":"Радиоантенна","Talked to the lander, never to Earth directly, which is why it stayed within about 12 m of it.":"Связывался с посадочным модулем, а не напрямую с Землёй, поэтому держался в пределах примерно 12 м от него.","Warm electronics box":"Тёплый отсек электроники","10.6 kg in total: the whole rover was about the size of a microwave oven.":"Всего 10,6 кг: весь марсоход был размером примерно с микроволновку.","Mission ended 1997":"Миссия завершена в 1997 году","Spirit rover’s solar-panel deck seen from above, lightly coated in dust":"Панели солнечных батарей марсохода Spirit сверху, слегка покрытые пылью","MARS ROVER · WORKED 2004–2010":"МАРСОХОД · РАБОТАЛ В 2004–2010 ГОДАХ","Built for a 90-day mission in Gusev Crater, it worked for more than six years. Its stuck wheel dug up nearly pure silica, the kind that forms around hot springs, a sign of a much wetter ancient Mars.":"Создан для 90-дневной миссии в кратере Гусев, а проработал больше шести лет. Его заклинившее колесо откопало почти чистый кремнезём, какой образуется у горячих источников, — признак гораздо более влажного древнего Марса.","planned mission":"запланированная миссия","6 yr 2 mo":"6 лет 2 мес.","actually worked":"проработал на деле","driven":"пройдено","longer than planned":"дольше запланированного","Study rocks and soil in Gusev Crater and look for clues that water once flowed there. The mission was planned for 90 Martian days.":"Изучать камни и грунт в кратере Гусев и искать признаки того, что там когда-то текла вода. Миссию планировали на 90 марсианских суток.","In the Columbia Hills: bedrock of many kinds, some of it changed by water.":"В холмах Колумбия: коренные породы многих видов, часть из них изменена водой.","At “Home Plate”: traces of an ancient volcano and explosive eruptions driven by hot underground water.":"У «Home Plate»: следы древнего вулкана и взрывных извержений, вызванных горячей подземной водой.","In 2007 its broken, dragging wheel dug up soil that was about 90% pure silica. On Earth this forms at hot springs and steam vents, so ancient Mars was much wetter.":"В 2007 году его сломанное колесо, которое он тащил за собой, вскрыло грунт почти на 90% из чистого кремнезёма. На Земле такой образуется у горячих источников и паровых выходов, значит, древний Марс был гораздо влажнее.","In the “Comanche” rocks: about ten times more carbonate than in any Martian rock studied before, a sign of water that was not acidic and could have suited life.":"В камнях «Команчи»: примерно в десять раз больше карбонатов, чем в любом изученном ранее марсианском камне, — признак некислой воды, которая могла подходить для жизни.","In 2005 it filmed dust devils moving across the plains.":"В 2005 году снял пылевые вихри, которые неслись по равнине.","Last contact on Mar. 22, 2010. Most likely the Martian winter grew too cold for its heaters.":"Последняя связь — 22 марта 2010 года. Скорее всего, марсианская зима стала слишком холодной для его обогревателей.","The rover is still physically on Mars, next to Home Plate.":"Марсоход до сих пор на Марсе, рядом с Home Plate.","Pancam mast":"Мачта с камерами Pancam","Colour panoramic cameras and navigation cameras on a mast about as tall as a person.":"Цветные панорамные и навигационные камеры на мачте высотой примерно с человека.","Solar panels":"Солнечные панели","They powered it for six years; the cold, dim Martian winter of 2009 to 2010 was too much.":"Они питали его шесть лет; холодная тёмная марсианская зима 2009–2010 годов оказалась слишком тяжёлой.","A steerable dish for talking straight to Earth.":"Поворотная тарелка для прямой связи с Землёй.","Robotic arm":"Манипулятор","Carries a microscopic imager, two spectrometers and a tool that ground into rocks to see inside them.":"Несёт микроскопическую камеру, два спектрометра и инструмент, который стачивал камни, чтобы заглянуть внутрь.","Six wheels":"Шесть колёс","Its right-front wheel stopped turning in 2006. Dragging it is how Spirit dug up nearly pure silica.":"Его правое переднее колесо перестало вращаться в 2006 году. Именно волоча его, Spirit откопал почти чистый кремнезём.","Keeps the computer and batteries warm through freezing Martian nights.":"Сохраняет компьютер и батареи в тепле морозными марсианскими ночами.","Mission ended 2011":"Миссия завершена в 2011 году","Opportunity rover self-portrait with clean solar panels on the reddish Martian surface":"Автопортрет марсохода Opportunity с чистыми солнечными панелями на красноватой поверхности Марса","MARS ROVER · WORKED 2004–2018":"МАРСОХОД · РАБОТАЛ В 2004–2018 ГОДАХ","Planned for 90 days, it explored Meridiani Planum for almost 15 years and drove 45 km. Hematite spherules and gypsum veins it found showed that liquid water once flowed on Mars.":"Рассчитанный на 90 дней, он почти 15 лет исследовал плато Меридиана и проехал 45 км. Найденные им гематитовые шарики и прожилки гипса показали, что на Марсе когда-то текла жидкая вода.","~15 years":"~15 лет","steepest slope climbed":"самый крутой склон, на который он поднялся","Find places on Mars where conditions may once have suited life, and look for signs of past water. The plan was 90 Martian days and 1 km of driving.":"Найти на Марсе места, где условия когда-то могли подходить для жизни, и искать следы древней воды. План — 90 марсианских суток и 1 км пути.","Small round grains of hematite, nicknamed “blueberries”. This mineral usually forms in water, but that water was acidic, which is hard on life.":"Маленькие круглые зёрна гематита, прозванные «черникой». Этот минерал обычно образуется в воде, но та вода была кислой — тяжёлые условия для жизни.","Bright veins of gypsum near Endeavour Crater, left by water flowing through cracks underground.":"Светлые прожилки гипса у кратера Индевор, оставленные водой, которая текла по подземным трещинам.","Clay minerals that formed in neutral water: the friendliest conditions for life of anywhere it went.":"Глинистые минералы, образовавшиеся в нейтральной воде, — самые благоприятные для жизни условия из всех мест, где он побывал.","In January 2005, an iron-nickel meteorite nicknamed “Heat Shield Rock”.":"В январе 2005 года — железо-никелевый метеорит по прозвищу «Heat Shield Rock».","Last contact on June 10, 2018.":"Последняя связь — 10 июня 2018 года.","Its 45.16 km driving record stood until Perseverance passed it on Oct. 11, 2026.":"Его рекорд пробега 45,16 км держался, пока Perseverance не побил его 11 октября 2026 года.","The rover is still physically on Mars, in Perseverance Valley on Endeavour Crater.":"Марсоход до сих пор на Марсе — в долине Персеверанс у кратера Индевор.","In 2018 a dust storm that covered the whole planet blocked the sunlight they needed.":"В 2018 году пылевая буря, накрывшая всю планету, закрыла нужный им солнечный свет.","They carried it 45.16 km, a record on another world until Perseverance passed it in 2026.":"Они пронесли его 45,16 км — рекорд на другой планете, пока Perseverance не побил его в 2026 году.","Mission ended 2019":"Миссия завершена в 2019 году","Perseverance rover selfie next to an arrowhead-shaped rock called Cheyava Falls":"Селфи марсохода Perseverance рядом с камнем в форме наконечника стрелы — «Чейава-Фоллс»","driven, a record":"пройдено, рекорд","Martian days at the record":"марсианских суток на момент рекорда","rock samples collected":"образцов пород собрано","extended mission end":"окончание расширенной миссии","Look for signs of ancient microbial life in Jezero Crater, study whether Mars could support life, collect rock and soil samples for a possible trip to Earth, and help prepare for human missions.":"Искать следы древней микробной жизни в кратере Езеро, изучать, мог ли Марс поддерживать жизнь, собирать образцы пород и грунта для возможной доставки на Землю и помогать готовить полёты людей.","Jezero Crater once held a lake, a river delta and rivers: a place that could have supported life.":"Когда-то в кратере Езеро были озеро, речная дельта и реки — место, где могла существовать жизнь.","The crater floor is made of two kinds of volcanic rock that were changed by water.":"Дно кратера сложено двумя видами вулканических пород, изменённых водой.","A 2024 sample from the rock “Cheyava Falls”, named “Sapphire Canyon”, holds potential biosignatures (published in Nature, Sept. 2025). These are clues, not proof: the same minerals can also form without life.":"Образец 2024 года из камня «Чейава-Фоллс» под названием «Сапфировый каньон» содержит возможные биосигнатуры (опубликовано в Nature в сентябре 2025). Это зацепки, а не доказательство: те же минералы могут образоваться и без жизни.","Its MOXIE experiment made oxygen from the carbon dioxide in Mars’ air.":"Его эксперимент MOXIE получал кислород из углекислого газа марсианского воздуха.","Its microphones made the first recordings of sound on the surface of Mars.":"Его микрофоны сделали первые записи звука на поверхности Марса.","On Oct. 11, 2026, its 2,006th Martian day, it passed Opportunity’s record: 45.22 km.":"11 октября 2026 года, на свой 2006-й марсианский день, он побил рекорд Opportunity: 45,22 км.","Its first extended mission runs from October 2026 to about the end of 2028, along the crater rim and south toward “Rainbow Falls”.":"Его первая расширенная миссия продлится с октября 2026 года примерно до конца 2028-го — вдоль края кратера и на юг, к «Rainbow Falls».","Limits: the biosignatures can only be confirmed in labs on Earth, and the sample return is not yet approved. When it drives toward the Sun, glare in its cameras makes it park by mid-afternoon.":"Ограничения: подтвердить биосигнатуры можно только в лабораториях на Земле, а доставка образцов ещё не одобрена. Когда он едет в сторону Солнца, блики в камерах заставляют его останавливаться уже к середине дня.","View from orbit of reddish ridged Martian ground with faint rover tracks and a tiny rover":"Вид с орбиты на красноватый ребристый грунт Марса с едва заметными следами и крошечным марсоходом","Seen from orbit on June 13, 2026 by the HiRISE camera: Perseverance is the small speck at the end of its tracks, a day before it passed the marathon distance.":"Снимок камеры HiRISE с орбиты 13 июня 2026 года: Perseverance — маленькая точка в конце своих следов, за день до того, как он прошёл марафонскую дистанцию.","Remote sensing mast":"Мачта дистанционного зондирования","Mastcam-Z, the zoom cameras, and SuperCam, which fires a laser at rocks to find out what they are made of.":"Mastcam-Z — камеры с зумом — и SuperCam, который стреляет лазером по камням, чтобы узнать, из чего они состоят.","Robotic arm and turret":"Манипулятор и турель","A 2.1 m arm carrying the coring drill and the PIXL and SHERLOC instruments that studied “Cheyava Falls”.":"Манипулятор длиной 2,1 м с керновым буром и приборами PIXL и SHERLOC, которые изучали «Чейава-Фоллс».","Sample handling":"Обработка образцов","Inside the front of the body, a small inner arm seals rock cores into tubes for a possible return to Earth.":"В передней части корпуса маленький внутренний манипулятор запечатывает керны в пробирки для возможной доставки на Землю.","Nuclear power source (MMRTG)":"Ядерный источник питания (MMRTG)","Turns the heat of decaying plutonium into electricity, day and night, whatever the dust.":"Превращает тепло распада плутония в электричество днём и ночью, какая бы ни была пыль.","The steerable dish that can talk to Earth directly; most data goes through orbiters overhead.":"Поворотная тарелка, способная связываться с Землёй напрямую; большая часть данных идёт через орбитальные аппараты над головой.","RIMFAX radar":"Радар RIMFAX","Ground-penetrating radar that maps the rock layers beneath the rover as it drives.":"Георадар, который на ходу составляет карту слоёв пород под марсоходом.","Front hazard cameras":"Передние камеры для объезда препятствий","Cameras that watch for rocks and holes in front of the wheels.":"Камеры, которые следят за камнями и ямами перед колёсами.","Wheels and rocker-bogie":"Колёса и подвеска «рокер-боги»","Six aluminium wheels on a suspension that keeps all of them on the ground; they have carried it more than 45 km.":"Шесть алюминиевых колёс на подвеске, которая держит их все на земле; они провезли его больше 45 км.","Rover body":"Корпус марсохода","The warm electronics box: computers, batteries, and MOXIE, the experiment that made oxygen on Mars.":"Тёплый отсек электроники: компьютеры, батареи и MOXIE — эксперимент, который получал кислород на Марсе.","Correct.":"Верно.","Next question":"Следующий вопрос","See your score":"Посмотреть результат","Good start. Read the glossary and the mission windows, then try again.":"Хорошее начало. Почитай словарь и окна миссий и попробуй снова.","Great work. A few more and you are an expert.":"Отличная работа. Ещё немного — и ты эксперт.","Perfect score. Mission control is impressed.":"Идеальный результат. Центр управления полётами впечатлён.","Play again":"Сыграть ещё раз","Without enough power to stay warm through the winter, it never woke up again.":"Без энергии, чтобы согреваться всю зиму, он больше так и не проснулся.","Scientists are careful: such patterns can sometimes form without life.":"Учёные осторожны: такие следы иногда образуются и без жизни.","Almost 12 times its plan.":"Почти в 12 раз дольше плана.","Engineers switch them off one by one to save power.":"Инженеры выключают их один за другим, чтобы экономить энергию.","In June 2018 the storm blocked the sunlight its solar panels needed.":"В июне 2018 года буря закрыла солнечный свет, нужный его солнечным панелям.","Water once filled the crater and a river built a delta there.":"Когда-то кратер заполняла вода, а река намыла там дельту.","On Aug. 25, 2012 it crossed the edge of the Sun’s heliosphere.":"25 августа 2012 года он пересёк границу гелиосферы Солнца.","It is more than 25 billion km away, almost one light-day.":"Он дальше 25 млрд км — почти один световой день.","It lasts 24 h 39 min 35 s.":"Он длится 24 ч 39 мин 35 с.","A record on another world for years, until Perseverance passed it.":"Рекорд на другой планете, державшийся годами, пока его не побил Perseverance.","It has no power at all, yet observatories still bounce lasers off it today.":"У него совсем нет питания, но обсерватории и сегодня отражают от него лазер.","It still sends data from interstellar space, but only 2 of its 10 instruments are on.":"Он всё ещё присылает данные из межзвёздного пространства, но включены только 2 из 10 его приборов.","It is still on Mars, but contact ended on Sept. 27, 1997.":"Он всё ещё на Марсе, но связь прервалась 27 сентября 1997 года.","It is still on Mars, stuck beside Home Plate; its last contact was in March 2010.":"Он всё ещё на Марсе, застрял рядом с Home Plate; последняя связь была в марте 2010 года.","It is still on Mars; it went silent in a planet-wide dust storm in June 2018.":"Он всё ещё на Марсе; он замолчал во время глобальной пылевой бури в июне 2018 года.","It is driving and collecting samples in Jezero Crater, on a mission extended to about 2028.":"Он ездит и собирает образцы в кратере Езеро; миссию продлили примерно до 2028 года.","Open in the glossary":"Открыть в словаре","Open in the glossary →":"Открыть в словаре →","Voyager 1 from Earth":"Voyager 1 от Земли","Perseverance has driven":"Perseverance проехал","Every claim has a source":"У каждого утверждения есть источник","Six objects":"Шесть аппаратов","Film":"Фильм","Screen":"Экран","NASA and JPL mission pages, NASA 3D models and photographs, the JPL Horizons ephemeris and NASA’s live Perseverance feeds.":"Страницы миссий NASA и JPL, 3D-модели и фотографии NASA, эфемериды JPL Horizons и живые ленты Perseverance от NASA.","Team Singularity’s · Team lead: Muzayana · Analyst · Engineer · Programmer":"Команда Singularity’s · Руководитель: Музаяна · Аналитик · Инженер · Программист","July 4, 1997. Mars Pathfinder lands in Ares Vallis, bouncing across the ground on giant airbags.":"4 июля 1997 года. Mars Pathfinder садится в долине Арес, подпрыгивая на гигантских надувных подушках.","The petals open, and Sojourner, a rover the size of a microwave oven, rolls down a ramp onto Mars.":"Лепестки раскрываются, и Sojourner, марсоход размером с микроволновку, съезжает по трапу на Марс.","But Sojourner had no radio strong enough to reach Earth. Every message went through the lander.":"Но у Sojourner не было радио, способного достать до Земли. Каждое сообщение шло через посадочный модуль.","It studied rocks the team named Yogi and Barnacle Bill. Planned for seven days, it worked for eighty-three.":"Он изучал камни, которые команда назвала «Йоги» и «Барнакл Билл». Его рассчитывали на семь дней, а он проработал восемьдесят три.","On September 27, 1997, the lander fell silent. Its battery had worn out, and without it the lander could not survive the freezing nights.":"27 сентября 1997 года посадочный модуль замолчал. Его батарея износилась, а без неё модуль не мог пережить морозные ночи.","Without the lander, Sojourner had no way to call home. It is still there in Ares Vallis, close to the lander that carried it.":"Без посадочного модуля Sojourner не мог связаться с домом. Он до сих пор в долине Арес, рядом с модулем, который его привёз.","Its idea lives on: every Mars rover since has six wheels on the same kind of suspension.":"Его идея живёт: у всех марсоходов после него шесть колёс на такой же подвеске.","January 2004. Spirit lands in Gusev Crater, built for a mission of ninety days.":"Январь 2004 года. Spirit садится в кратер Гусев. Его создали для миссии на девяносто дней.","In 2006 its right front wheel stopped turning. Spirit learned to drive backwards, dragging the broken wheel.":"В 2006 году его правое переднее колесо перестало вращаться. Spirit научился ездить задним ходом, волоча сломанное колесо.","The dragged wheel scraped up almost pure silica, a sign that hot springs once bubbled here.":"Волочащееся колесо соскребло почти чистый кремнезём — признак того, что когда-то здесь били горячие источники.","In May 2009, at a place called Troy, its wheels broke through a crust into soft sand. Spirit was stuck.":"В мае 2009 года в месте под названием Троя его колёса проломили корку и ушли в мягкий песок. Spirit застрял.","Engineers practised escape drives with a test rover in a sandbox on Earth. But winter was coming, and Spirit could not tilt its panels toward the low Sun.":"Инженеры отрабатывали манёвры спасения на тестовом марсоходе в песочнице на Земле. Но приближалась зима, а Spirit не мог наклонить панели к низкому Солнцу.","Too cold and too weak to stay awake, Spirit went silent. Its last message arrived on March 22, 2010.":"Слишком замёрзший и ослабевший, чтобы бодрствовать, Spirit замолчал. Его последнее сообщение пришло 22 марта 2010 года.","NASA listened for more than a year before ending the mission in May 2011. Ninety days had become six years.":"NASA слушала больше года, прежде чем завершить миссию в мае 2011 года. Девяносто дней превратились в шесть лет.","January 2004. Three weeks after its twin Spirit, Opportunity lands on Meridiani Planum.":"Январь 2004 года. Через три недели после своего близнеца Spirit на плато Меридиана садится Opportunity.","It found tiny grey spheres of hematite, nicknamed blueberries, that formed in water long ago.":"Он нашёл крошечные серые шарики гематита — их прозвали «черникой», — которые давным-давно образовались в воде.","Over fourteen years it drove forty-five kilometres, a marathon on another world.":"За четырнадцать лет он проехал сорок пять километров — марафон на другой планете.","June 2018. A dust storm grows until it wraps the whole planet. Day turns into night.":"Июнь 2018 года. Пылевая буря разрастается, пока не окутывает всю планету. День превращается в ночь.","With almost no sunlight reaching its solar panels, Opportunity could not make enough power to keep talking.":"Почти без солнечного света на панелях Opportunity не мог вырабатывать достаточно энергии, чтобы оставаться на связи.","Its last message came on June 10, 2018. Engineers sent more than a thousand commands, but no answer came back.":"Его последнее сообщение пришло 10 июня 2018 года. Инженеры отправили больше тысячи команд, но ответа так и не было.","NASA ended the mission on February 13, 2019. It had been planned for ninety days. It lasted almost fifteen years.":"NASA завершила миссию 13 февраля 2019 года. Её планировали на девяносто дней. Она длилась почти пятнадцать лет.","September 5, 1977. Voyager 1 lifts off from Florida on a Titan rocket.":"5 сентября 1977 года. Voyager 1 стартует из Флориды на ракете «Титан».","It flies past Jupiter in 1979 and Saturn in 1980, using their gravity to speed on.":"Он пролетает мимо Юпитера в 1979 году и Сатурна в 1980-м, используя их притяжение, чтобы разогнаться.","In 1990, from six billion kilometres, it looks back and takes the Pale Blue Dot: Earth, smaller than a pixel.":"В 1990 году с расстояния шести миллиардов километров он оглядывается и делает снимок «Бледно-голубая точка»: Земля меньше пикселя.","In 2012 it leaves the heliosphere, the bubble of the solar wind, and becomes the first craft in interstellar space.":"В 2012 году он покидает гелиосферу — пузырь солнечного ветра — и становится первым аппаратом в межзвёздном пространстве.","Out here sunlight is too weak for solar panels. Its power comes from plutonium generators, and they lose about four watts every year.":"Здесь солнечный свет слишком слаб для солнечных панелей. Энергию дают плутониевые генераторы, и они теряют около четырёх ватт каждый год.","To save power, engineers switch its instruments off one by one. Today only two of its ten are still on.":"Чтобы экономить энергию, инженеры выключают его приборы один за другим. Сегодня включены только два из десяти.","Its signal now takes almost a day to reach us. Giant dishes like these in Madrid still listen for it.":"Теперь его сигнал идёт до нас почти сутки. Гигантские антенны, как эти в Мадриде, всё ещё слушают его.","Which object has no power at all, yet is still used every year?":"Какой аппарат совсем без питания, но всё ещё используется каждый год?","It is a passive mirror: observatories fire lasers at it and time the echo.":"Это пассивное зеркало: обсерватории посылают в него лазер и засекают время отражения.","How long does a laser pulse take to reach the Moon and come back?":"Сколько времени лазерный импульс летит до Луны и обратно?","About 2.5 seconds":"Около 2,5 секунды","About 0.25 seconds":"Около 0,25 секунды","About 25 seconds":"Около 25 секунд","About 4 minutes":"Около 4 минут","The Moon is about 384,000 km away; light covers that twice in roughly 2.5 s.":"Луна примерно в 384 000 км; свет проходит это расстояние дважды примерно за 2,5 с.","What ended Opportunity’s mission?":"Что завершило миссию Opportunity?","A dust storm that covered the whole planet":"Пылевая буря, накрывшая всю планету","It got stuck in soft sand":"Застрял в мягком песке","Its plutonium ran out":"У него кончился плутоний","How far did Opportunity drive on Mars?":"Сколько проехал Opportunity по Марсу?","Why did Spirit go silent in 2010?":"Почему Spirit замолчал в 2010 году?","Stuck in sand, it could not tilt its solar panels toward the winter Sun":"Застряв в песке, он не мог наклонить солнечные панели к зимнему Солнцу","A meteorite hit it":"В него попал метеорит","A dust storm buried it":"Его засыпала пылевая буря","Its antenna broke off":"У него отломилась антенна","What did Spirit’s broken, dragging wheel dig up?":"Что откопало сломанное, волочащееся колесо Spirit?","Nearly pure silica":"Почти чистый кремнезём","Ice":"Лёд","Gold":"Золото","A fossil":"Окаменелость","Silica like this forms around hot springs: a sign of a wetter, warmer past.":"Такой кремнезём образуется у горячих источников — признак более влажного и тёплого прошлого.","How did Sojourner send its data to Earth?":"Как Sojourner отправлял данные на Землю?","Through its lander’s radio":"Через радио посадочного модуля","Straight to Earth with its own dish":"Напрямую на Землю через свою антенну","Through an orbiter":"Через орбитальный аппарат","It stored it to be collected later":"Сохранял их, чтобы забрали позже","That is why it ended when the Pathfinder lander fell silent.":"Поэтому он и замолчал, когда умолк посадочный модуль Pathfinder.","Sojourner was planned for 7 days. How long did it work?":"Sojourner рассчитывали на 7 дней. Сколько он проработал?","83 days":"83 дня","7 days":"7 дней","1 year":"1 год","14 years":"14 лет","When did Voyager 1 enter interstellar space?":"Когда Voyager 1 вошёл в межзвёздное пространство?","What powers Voyager 1?":"Что питает Voyager 1?","Plutonium generators (RTGs)":"Плутониевые генераторы (РИТЭГи)","Batteries charged from Earth":"Батареи, заряженные с Земли","A small rocket engine":"Небольшой ракетный двигатель","Sunlight is far too weak out there. The RTGs lose about 4 W a year.":"Солнечный свет там слишком слаб. РИТЭГи теряют около 4 Вт в год.","How many of Voyager 1’s ten instruments are still switched on?":"Сколько из десяти приборов Voyager 1 ещё включены?","How long does Voyager 1’s radio signal take to reach Earth?":"Сколько идёт радиосигнал Voyager 1 до Земли?","Almost a whole day":"Почти целые сутки","About 8 minutes":"Около 8 минут","About 4 hours":"Около 4 часов","About a week":"Около недели","What did Perseverance find in the rock “Cheyava Falls”?":"Что Perseverance нашёл в камне «Чейава-Фоллс»?","Potential biosignatures: clues, not proof of life":"Возможные биосигнатуры: зацепки, а не доказательство жизни","Living bacteria":"Живые бактерии","Liquid water":"Жидкую воду","Nothing unusual":"Ничего необычного","Where is Perseverance exploring?":"Где исследует Perseverance?","Jezero Crater, an ancient lake bed":"Кратер Езеро — дно древнего озера","The Sea of Tranquility":"Море Спокойствия","Olympus Mons":"Гора Олимп","Which was the first wheeled vehicle on another planet?":"Какая машина первой поехала на колёсах по другой планете?","It rolled onto Mars in July 1997.":"Он съехал на Марс в июле 1997 года.","What is a sol?":"Что такое сол?","A day on Mars":"Сутки на Марсе","A Martian year":"Марсианский год","A unit of power":"Единица мощности","A type of rock":"Вид горной породы","Mars Pathfinder":"Mars Pathfinder","Ares Vallis":"Долина Арес","Sojourner’s own view: its wheel, lower left":"Вид с камеры Sojourner: его колесо внизу слева","The only link home":"Единственная связь с домом","rover → lander → Earth":"марсоход → посадочный модуль → Земля","Days working":"Дней в работе","Planned":"План","Lander battery":"Батарея модуля","January 2004: looking back at its lander":"Январь 2004: взгляд назад, на посадочный модуль","One wheel stuck: the drag marks":"Одно колесо заклинило: следы волочения","The bright soil, 2007":"Светлый грунт, 2007","Troy":"Троя","Soil churned by escape attempts":"Грунт, взрытый попытками выбраться","Spirit’s power":"Энергия Spirit","January 2004":"Январь 2004","Hematite “blueberries”":"Гематитовая «черника»","Microscope view, a few millimetres each":"Под микроскопом, по несколько миллиметров каждая","Distance driven":"Пройдено","The storm seen from orbit":"Буря с орбиты","Sunlight":"Солнечный свет","Power":"Энергия","Commands sent":"Отправлено команд","Replies":"Ответов","Cape Canaveral":"Мыс Канаверал","January 1979":"Январь 1979","November 1980":"Ноябрь 1980","Interstellar space (illustration)":"Межзвёздное пространство (иллюстрация)","Year":"Год","Electrical power":"Электрическая мощность","Instruments on":"Включено приборов","One-way light time":"Время сигнала в одну сторону","Why it went silent":"Почему он замолчал","Why it is limited":"Почему он ограничен","Planned: 7":"План: 7","6 years":"6 лет","Planned: 90 days":"План: 90 дней","instruments still on · still sending data":"приборов включено · данные всё ещё идут","Achievement unlocked":"Достижение открыто","Space ambience and shooting stars. Adjust it in Settings.":"Космический фон и падающие звёзды. Настроить можно в настройках.","Lighter device detected":"Похоже, устройство не самое мощное","Use 2D photos instead of 3D models for smoother scrolling?":"Использовать 2D-фото вместо 3D-моделей для более плавной прокрутки?","Use 2D":"Включить 2D","Keep 3D":"Оставить 3D","Saving mobile data":"Экономия мобильного трафика","Showing NASA photos instead of the 3D models (about 12 MB each).":"Показываем фото NASA вместо 3D-моделей (около 12 МБ каждая).","Load 3D":"Загрузить 3D","Keep photos":"Оставить фото","Progress reset":"Прогресс сброшен","Your achievements start again.":"Достижения начинаются заново.","Reset all achievements and progress on this device?":"Сбросить все достижения и прогресс на этом устройстве?","Fact":"Факт","Quiz":"Квиз","watched":"просмотрено","Language":"Язык","Click for its key facts":"Нажмите, чтобы увидеть главные факты","Our planet · home of all six missions":"Наша планета · дом всех шести миссий","35° above the planets":"на 35° выше планет","You are here":"Вы здесь","Mercury":"Меркурий","Venus":"Венера","Earth":"Земля","Uranus":"Уран","Neptune":"Нептун","Rocky planet · 1st from the Sun":"Каменистая планета · 1-я от Солнца","Rocky planet · 2nd from the Sun":"Каменистая планета · 2-я от Солнца","Rocky planet · 3rd from the Sun":"Каменистая планета · 3-я от Солнца","Rocky planet · 4th from the Sun":"Каменистая планета · 4-я от Солнца","Gas giant · 5th from the Sun":"Газовый гигант · 5-я от Солнца","Gas giant · 6th from the Sun":"Газовый гигант · 6-я от Солнца","Ice giant · 7th from the Sun":"Ледяной гигант · 7-я от Солнца","Ice giant · 8th from the Sun":"Ледяной гигант · 8-я от Солнца","A small, rocky world with a heavily cratered surface. It has almost no atmosphere and swings between extreme heat and cold.":"Маленький каменистый мир с поверхностью, сплошь покрытой кратерами. Атмосферы почти нет, и там то страшная жара, то лютый холод.","A dense carbon-dioxide atmosphere and thick clouds trap heat, making it the hottest planet in the Solar System.":"Плотная атмосфера из углекислого газа и густые облака удерживают тепло, поэтому это самая горячая планета Солнечной системы.","Our home world has liquid water on its surface and a nitrogen-oxygen atmosphere. It is the only world known to support life.":"На нашем родном мире есть жидкая вода на поверхности и азотно-кислородная атмосфера. Это единственный известный мир, где есть жизнь.","A cold desert world with ancient river valleys, polar ice and the largest volcano known in the Solar System. Rovers study whether it was once habitable.":"Холодная пустыня с древними речными долинами, полярными льдами и самым большим известным вулканом Солнечной системы. Марсоходы выясняют, была ли она когда-то пригодна для жизни.","The largest planet, a gas giant with huge storms such as the Great Red Spot. Its moon Io is the most volcanic world known.":"Самая большая планета, газовый гигант с огромными бурями вроде Большого красного пятна. Его спутник Ио — самый вулканически активный известный мир.","Famous for bright rings made mostly of ice. Its moon Titan has a thick, mostly nitrogen atmosphere that hides its surface.":"Знаменит яркими кольцами, в основном изо льда. У его спутника Титана плотная, в основном азотная атмосфера, скрывающая поверхность.","An ice giant that spins on a strongly tilted axis. Methane in its atmosphere gives it a blue-green colour.":"Ледяной гигант, вращающийся на сильно наклонённой оси. Метан в атмосфере придаёт ему сине-зелёный цвет.","A distant ice giant with very fast winds and a deep blue colour.":"Далёкий ледяной гигант с очень быстрыми ветрами и насыщенным синим цветом.","None of our six":"Ни одного из наших шести","All six started here. The Apollo 11 reflector sits on its Moon.":"Все шесть стартовали отсюда. Отражатель Apollo 11 стоит на её Луне.","Sojourner, Spirit, Opportunity, Perseverance":"Sojourner, Spirit, Opportunity, Perseverance","Voyager 1 flew past in March 1979":"Voyager 1 пролетел мимо в марте 1979 года","Voyager 1 flew past in November 1980":"Voyager 1 пролетел мимо в ноябре 1980 года","None of our six (Voyager 2 flew past in 1986)":"Ни одного из наших шести (Voyager 2 пролетел мимо в 1986 году)","None of our six (Voyager 2 flew past in 1989)":"Ни одного из наших шести (Voyager 2 пролетел мимо в 1989 году)","Loading…":"Загрузка…","Jezero Crater rim":"край кратера Езеро","western rim of Jezero Crater":"западный край кратера Езеро","NASA Mars Pathfinder mission pages and photographs":"страниц миссии Mars Pathfinder и фотографий NASA","NASA Mars Exploration Rover mission pages and photographs":"страниц миссии Mars Exploration Rover и фотографий NASA","NASA and JPL Voyager mission pages and photographs":"страниц миссии Voyager и фотографий NASA и JPL","Terms":"Термины"},"uz":{"Triple-click to hide the text":"Matnni yashirish uchun uch marta bosing","Show text":"Matnni ko‘rsatish","Team Singularity":"Singularity jamoasi","Team Singularity · Team lead: Muzayana · Analyst · Engineer · Programmer":"Singularity jamoasi · Jamoa rahbari: Muzayana · Tahlilchi · Muhandis · Dasturchi","Pages":"Sahifalar","Missions":"Missiyalar","Explore":"Tadqiq qilish","Learn":"O‘rganish","Compare":"Solishtirish","Glossary":"Lug‘at","Search the site":"Saytdan qidirish","Search (Ctrl K)":"Qidirish (Ctrl K)","Turn sound on":"Ovozni yoqish","Turn sound off":"Ovozni o‘chirish","Sound off":"Ovoz o‘chiq","Sound on":"Ovoz yoqiq","Settings":"Sozlamalar","Open navigation":"Menyuni ochish","Close navigation":"Menyuni yopish","3D model of Perseverance. Drag, or use the arrow keys while focused, to turn it.":"Perseverance 3D modeli. Aylantirish uchun suring yoki strelka tugmalarini bosing.","The 3D model could not load, so you are seeing the NASA photo.":"3D model yuklanmadi, shuning uchun NASA surati ko‘rsatilmoqda.","Try again":"Qayta urinish","The mission may end. The evidence remains.":"Missiya tugashi mumkin. Dalillar qoladi.","Six NASA explorers: what they left behind, and whether it still works.":"NASAning olti tadqiqotchisi: ular nimani qoldirgan va u hali ham ishlaydimi.","MARS ROVER · ON MARS SINCE 2021":"MARSOXOD · 2021-YILDAN BERI MARSDA","Exploring Jezero Crater, an ancient lake bed, and collecting rock samples for a possible return to Earth. In 2024 it found potential biosignatures in the rock “Cheyava Falls”: intriguing clues, not proof of life.":"Qadimiy ko‘l tubi bo‘lgan Jezero kraterini o‘rganadi va Yerga olib kelish mumkin bo‘lgan tosh namunalarini yig‘adi. 2024-yilda “Cheyava Falls” toshida ehtimoliy biosignaturalarni topdi: qiziqarli belgilar, lekin hayot isboti emas.","Launched":"Uchirilgan","Where now":"Hozir qayerda","Jezero Crater rim, Mars":"Jezero krateri cheti, Mars","Status":"Holati","Active, to about 2028":"Ishlayapti, taxminan 2028-yilgacha","Choose a spacecraft":"Apparatni tanlang","LEARN MORE":"BATAFSIL","Drag the model to turn it":"Modelni aylantirish uchun suring","Image":"Surat","Illustration":"Illyustratsiya","3D model:":"3D model:","Scroll to the next section":"Keyingi bo‘limga o‘tish","Missions: sections":"Missiyalar: bo‘limlar","The idea":"G‘oya","Live now":"Hozir","What does a spacecraft leave behind?":"Kosmik apparat o‘zidan keyin nima qoldiradi?","Six pieces of hardware, from a mirror the size of a suitcase on the Moon to a probe beyond the Sun’s influence. For each one: where it is, why it was built, what it taught us, whether it still works, and where to check. The mission may end. The evidence remains.":"Oltita apparat: Oydagi chamadon kattaligidagi oynadan tortib Quyosh ta’siridan tashqaridagi zondgacha. Har biri haqida: qayerda, nima uchun qurilgan, bizga nimani o‘rgatgan, hali ishlaydimi va buni qayerdan tekshirish mumkin. Missiya tugashi mumkin. Dalillar qoladi.","years since Armstrong and Aldrin left the Apollo 11 reflector on the Moon. Observatories still fire lasers at it.":"yil oldin Armstrong va Oldrin Apollo 11 qaytargichini Oyda qoldirishgan. Observatoriyalar unga hozir ham lazer yuboradi.","years since Voyager 1 launched. It is still sending data from interstellar space.":"yil oldin Voyager 1 uchirilgan. U hali ham yulduzlararo fazodan ma’lumot yuboradi.","days Sojourner worked on Mars, against a plan of 7.":"kun Sojourner Marsda ishladi, reja esa 7 kun edi.","years Spirit worked on Mars, on a mission planned for 90 days.":"yil Spirit Marsda ishladi, missiya esa 90 kunga mo‘ljallangan edi.","years Opportunity worked on Mars, on a mission planned for 90 days.":"yil Opportunity Marsda ishladi, missiya esa 90 kunga mo‘ljallangan edi.","km driven by Perseverance, a record on another world. It is still driving.":"km yo‘l bosdi Perseverance — boshqa sayyoradagi rekord. U hali ham harakatlanmoqda.","Where they are, this second":"Ular aynan hozir qayerda","Perseverance’s figures come live from NASA’s mission feed. The Moon and Voyager 1 are calculated every second from JPL data. The silent rovers count the days since their last contact.":"Perseverance ma’lumotlari NASA missiyasi lentasidan jonli keladi. Oy va Voyager 1 har soniyada JPL ma’lumotlari asosida hisoblanadi. Jim qolgan marsoxodlar uchun oxirgi aloqadan beri o‘tgan kunlar sanaladi.","Exists or works? The four status labels":"Mavjudmi yoki ishlaydimi? To‘rtta holat","Exists or works?":"Mavjudmi yoki ishlaydimi?","Operating":"Ishlayapti","Active and returning science.":"Ishlayapti va ilmiy ma’lumot yubormoqda.","Passive, still used":"Passiv, hali ham foydalaniladi","No power at all, yet still part of today’s measurements.":"Umuman quvvatsiz, lekin bugungi o‘lchovlarda hali ham qatnashadi.","Transmitting, limited":"Ma’lumot yuboradi, cheklangan","Still sending data, with fewer instruments switched on.":"Hali ham ma’lumot yuboradi, lekin kamroq asbob yoqilgan.","On surface, not working":"Sirtda, ishlamaydi","Still there, no longer operating.":"Hali ham o‘sha yerda, lekin endi ishlamaydi.","Apollo 11 laser retroreflector":"Apollo 11 lazer qaytargichi","Calculated · JPL data":"Hisoblangan · JPL ma’lumotlari","Earth–Moon distance now":"Hozirgi Yer–Oy masofasi","A laser pulse there and back takes":"Lazer impulsining borib-kelishi","Since Eagle landed (July 20, 1969, 20:17 UTC)":"Eagle qo‘nganidan beri (1969-yil 20-iyul, 20:17 UTC)","Moon distance computed with Meeus’ lunar theory, checked against":"Oygacha masofa Meeus oy nazariyasi bo‘yicha hisoblangan va quyidagi bilan solishtirilgan:","to within 20 km.":"20 km aniqlikda.","See it in 3D":"3D’da ko‘rish","Distance from Earth now":"Hozir Yerdan masofa","From the Sun":"Quyoshdan","Its radio signal needs":"Uning radiosignaliga kerak","Moving away from the Sun at":"Quyoshdan uzoqlashish tezligi","Interpolated from":"Interpolyatsiya manbai:","every second.":"har soniyada.","Counted from last contact":"Oxirgi aloqadan beri sanalgan","Silent for":"Jim qolganiga","That is about":"Bu taxminan","Last data from Mars":"Marsdan oxirgi ma’lumot","Worked":"Ishladi","83 days, against a plan of 7":"83 kun, reja esa 7 kun edi","Last contact":"Oxirgi aloqa","Drove":"Yo‘l bosdi","7.73 km on a 90-day mission":"90 kunlik missiyada 7,73 km","45.16 km on a 90-day mission":"90 kunlik missiyada 45,16 km","Live · NASA feed":"Jonli · NASA lentasi","Driven on Mars":"Marsda bosib o‘tgan yo‘li","Latest drive":"Oxirgi harakat","Where it is":"Qayerda","Mission day now (sol)":"Hozirgi missiya kuni (sol)","Live from NASA’s":"NASA’ning jonli","mission map":"missiya xaritasi","and":"va","raw images":"xom suratlar","feeds.":"lentalaridan.","· Updated every second. Spirit, Opportunity and Sojourner count from their last contact, not from a known moment of failure.":"· Har soniyada yangilanadi. Spirit, Opportunity va Sojourner uchun hisob oxirgi aloqadan boshlanadi, aniq buzilish vaqtidan emas.","The real Solar System, today":"Bugungi haqiqiy Quyosh tizimi","Where every object is right now, the planets in their true positions for today’s date, and the photographs that prove it.":"Har bir apparat aynan hozir qayerda, sayyoralar bugungi sanadagi haqiqiy joylarida va buni isbotlaydigan suratlar.","Explore: sections":"Tadqiq qilish: bo‘limlar","Map":"Xarita","Photos":"Suratlar","Fly the evidence trail":"Dalillar izidan yuring","Where all six really are today, worked out from NASA and JPL data. Distances are squeezed so the planets fit; Voyager 1, about 170 times farther from the Sun than Earth, sits past a break in the scale. Tap a glowing pin to open that object, or a planet for its key facts.":"Oltitasi ham bugun aslida qayerda ekani NASA va JPL ma’lumotlari asosida. Sayyoralar sig‘ishi uchun masofalar qisqartirilgan; Quyoshdan Yerga nisbatan taxminan 170 marta uzoqroqdagi Voyager 1 shkala uzilishidan keyin turibdi. Apparatni ochish uchun yonib turgan nuqtani, asosiy faktlar uchun sayyorani bosing.","Map of the Solar System for today's date, with the six objects pinned at their real directions from the Sun. Use the buttons under the map to open an object.":"Bugungi sana uchun Quyosh tizimi xaritasi: oltita apparat Quyoshdan haqiqiy yo‘nalishlari bo‘yicha belgilangan. Apparatni ochish uchun xarita ostidagi tugmalardan foydalaning.","Voyager 1 right now · JPL Horizons":"Voyager 1 aynan hozir · JPL Horizons","Check NASA’s live figure ↗":"NASA’ning jonli ko‘rsatkichi bilan solishtirish ↗","Time travel":"Vaqt bo‘ylab sayohat","Days from today":"Bugundan boshlab kunlar","Today":"Bugun","Play":"Ijro etish","Pause":"Pauza","Close the planet facts":"Sayyora faktlarini yopish","Planet":"Sayyora","Mean distance from the Sun":"Quyoshdan o‘rtacha masofa","One orbit (a year)":"Bir aylanish (bir yil)","Diameter":"Diametri","Known moons":"Ma’lum yo‘ldoshlar","Visited by our objects":"Bizning apparatlarimizdan kim borgan","From Earth on this date":"Bu sanada Yerdan masofa","Moon counts are NASA’s as of 2026 (Saturn 293, Jupiter 115 recognised by the IAU, Uranus 29) and keep growing.":"Yo‘ldoshlar soni NASA’ning 2026-yilgi ma’lumotlariga ko‘ra (Saturn 293, Yupiter XAI tan olgan 115 ta, Uran 29) va u o‘sishda davom etmoqda.","Planet positions are calculated for the chosen date from JPL’s orbital elements (accurate to a fraction of a degree). Voyager 1 is interpolated from the JPL Horizons ephemeris, and the Moon’s distance comes from Meeus’ lunar theory. Directions are true; distances are compressed.":"Sayyoralarning joylashuvi tanlangan sana uchun JPL orbital elementlari bo‘yicha hisoblanadi (gradusning bir qismigacha aniqlikda). Voyager 1 JPL Horizons efemeridalari bo‘yicha interpolyatsiya qilingan, Oygacha masofa esa Meeus oy nazariyasidan olingan. Yo‘nalishlar haqiqiy, masofalar qisqartirilgan.","Evidence you can see":"Ko‘rish mumkin bo‘lgan dalillar","Real photographs from the Moon, Mars and deep space, each with what it proves. Click any picture to enlarge it.":"Oy, Mars va uzoq koinotdan haqiqiy suratlar — har biri nimani isbotlashi bilan. Kattalashtirish uchun suratni bosing.","Buzz Aldrin beside the laser reflector he had just set up, July 20, 1969. Proof it is there: observatories still bounce lasers off it today.":"Bazz Oldrin endigina o‘rnatgan lazer qaytargichi yonida, 1969-yil 20-iyul. U o‘sha yerda ekanining isboti: observatoriyalar bugun ham undan lazerni qaytaradi.","Eagle, the Lunar Module that carried the reflector to the Moon. Its lower half is still standing at Tranquility Base.":"Eagle — qaytargichni Oyga olib borgan oy moduli. Uning pastki qismi hali ham Osoyishtalik bazasida turibdi.","Earth from lunar orbit. The Moon always keeps the same face towards us, so the reflector sees Earth in the same part of its sky.":"Oy orbitasidan Yer. Oy bizga doim bir tomoni bilan qaragan, shuning uchun qaytargich Yerni osmonining bir xil qismida ko‘radi.","Apollo 15, two years later, left a bigger reflector with 300 prisms. Observatories range to the Apollo arrays together.":"Apollo 15 ikki yildan keyin 300 ta prizmali kattaroq qaytargich qoldirdi. Observatoriyalar barcha Apollo qaytargichlarigacha masofani birga o‘lchaydi.","The “Pale Blue Dot”, Feb. 14, 1990: Earth from about 6 billion km. Voyager 1’s cameras were switched off soon after to save power.":"“Xira ko‘k nuqta”, 1990-yil 14-fevral: taxminan 6 mlrd km masofadan Yer. Shundan so‘ng tez orada quvvatni tejash uchun Voyager 1 kameralari o‘chirildi.","Sojourner pressing its spectrometer against the rock “Yogi”: the first chemical analysis of a rock by a rover on Mars.":"Sojourner spektrometrini “Yogi” toshiga bosmoqda: Marsda marsoxod tomonidan toshning birinchi kimyoviy tahlili.","The Pathfinder lander, Sojourner’s only radio link to Earth. When its battery gave out in 1997, the rover went silent too.":"Pathfinder qo‘nish moduli — Sojournerning Yer bilan yagona radioaloqasi. 1997-yilda uning batareyasi ishdan chiqqach, marsoxod ham jim qoldi.","Spirit’s solar panels in 2005, dusty after two years. All its power came from sunlight on this deck, the weakness that ended it.":"Spiritning quyosh panellari 2005-yilda, ikki yilda changga botgan. Uning butun quvvati shu panellarga tushgan quyosh nuridan kelgan — bu uning zaif joyi bo‘ldi.","Opportunity in 2014, after wind had cleaned its panels. Clean panels kept it going for years, until the 2018 dust storm.":"Opportunity 2014-yilda, shamol panellarini tozalagandan keyin. Toza panellar uni yillar davomida ishlatib turdi — 2018-yilgi chang bo‘ronigacha.","Perseverance beside “Cheyava Falls”, July 2024: the rock whose potential biosignatures are now being studied.":"Perseverance “Cheyava Falls” yonida, 2024-yil iyul: ehtimoliy biosignaturalari hozir o‘rganilayotgan tosh.","Rocks in Jezero Crater beside a Perseverance wheel. The crater was once a lake, which is why the rover was sent here.":"Jezero kraterida Perseverance g‘ildiragi yonidagi toshlar. Krater bir vaqtlar ko‘l bo‘lgan — marsoxod shuning uchun shu yerga yuborilgan.","Perseverance seen from orbit by HiRISE, June 13, 2026: an independent check that it is where NASA says.":"HiRISE kamerasi orbitadan ko‘rgan Perseverance, 2026-yil 13-iyun: u NASA aytgan joyda ekanining mustaqil tekshiruvi.","How do we know?":"Buni qayerdan bilamiz?","Fifty-seven years of evidence, every claim with its evidence and its limits, four short films and a test.":"Ellik yetti yillik dalillar, har bir da’vo o‘z dalillari va cheklovlari bilan, to‘rtta qisqa film va test.","Learn: sections":"O‘rganish: bo‘limlar","Timeline":"Xronologiya","Evidence lab":"Dalillar laboratoriyasi","Films":"Filmlar","Test yourself":"O‘zingizni sinang","Achievements":"Yutuqlar","57 years of evidence":"57 yillik dalillar","From the first moonwalk to an off-world driving record, year by year. Each event is marked with the object it belongs to.":"Oydagi birinchi sayrdan boshqa sayyoradagi yo‘l rekordigacha, yilma-yil. Har bir voqea qaysi apparatga tegishli ekani belgilangan.","Apollo 11 launches from Kennedy Space Center, Florida.":"Apollo 11 Floridadagi Kennedi kosmik markazidan uchiriladi.","Apollo 11 reflector":"Apollo 11 qaytargichi","Armstrong and Aldrin land in the Sea of Tranquility and walk on the Moon.":"Armstrong va Oldrin Osoyishtalik dengiziga qo‘nib, Oy bo‘ylab yurishadi.","The reflector is set up near the end of the moonwalk (UTC date).":"Qaytargich Oy sirtidagi sayrning oxirida o‘rnatiladi (UTC sanasi).","Apollo 14 and Apollo 15 leave two more reflector arrays.":"Apollo 14 va Apollo 15 yana ikkita qaytargich qoldiradi.","Launched from Cape Canaveral, Florida.":"Floridadagi Kanaveral burnidan uchirilgan.","Voyager 2 launches, two weeks before Voyager 1.":"Voyager 2 uchiriladi — Voyager 1 dan ikki hafta oldin.","Closest approach to Jupiter.":"Yupiterga eng yaqin kelish.","Voyager 1 pictures reveal volcanoes erupting on Io, a moon of Jupiter.":"Voyager 1 suratlari Yupiterning yo‘ldoshi Ioda otilayotgan vulqonlarni ko‘rsatadi.","Closest approach to Saturn and Titan.":"Saturn va Titanga eng yaqin kelish.","Takes the “Pale Blue Dot”; cameras are switched off.":"“Xira ko‘k nuqta” suratini oladi; kameralar o‘chiriladi.","Mars Pathfinder launches from Cape Canaveral, Florida.":"Mars Pathfinder Floridadagi Kanaveral burnidan uchiriladi.","Lands in Ares Vallis, bouncing on airbags.":"Havo yostiqlarida sakrab, Ares vodiysiga qo‘nadi.","Sojourner rolls down a ramp onto Mars.":"Sojourner trap orqali Marsga tushadi.","Studies its first rocks, “Barnacle Bill” and “Yogi”.":"O‘zining birinchi toshlari — “Barnacle Bill” va “Yogi”ni o‘rganadi.","Last data from the mission.":"Missiyadan oxirgi ma’lumot.","After 35 years, ranging is accurate to about 2 cm.":"35 yildan keyin masofa o‘lchash aniqligi taxminan 2 sm.","Lands in Gusev Crater.":"Gusev krateriga qo‘nadi.","Lands in Eagle crater, Meridiani Planum (US time).":"Meridiani Planumdagi Eagle krateriga qo‘nadi (AQSh vaqti bilan).","Films dust devils in motion.":"Harakatdagi chang quyunlarini suratga oladi.","Finds the “Heat Shield Rock” meteorite.":"“Heat Shield Rock” meteoritini topadi.","Finds nearly pure silica.":"Deyarli sof kremnezyomni topadi.","Gets stuck in soft soil.":"Yumshoq gruntga botib qoladi.","Last contact with Earth.":"Yer bilan oxirgi aloqa.","NASA ends the mission.":"NASA missiyani yakunlaydi.","Reaches Endeavour Crater.":"Endeavour kraterigacha yetib boradi.","Crosses the heliopause into interstellar space.":"Geliopauzani kesib o‘tib, yulduzlararo fazoga chiqadi.","Drives on a 32° slope, the steepest for any Mars rover.":"32° qiyalikda yuradi — bu marsoxodlar uchun eng tik qiyalik.","Last contact, during a planet-wide dust storm.":"Oxirgi aloqa — butun sayyorani qoplagan chang bo‘roni paytida.","After 50 years, measurements reach a few millimetres.":"50 yildan keyin o‘lchovlar aniqligi bir necha millimetrga yetadi.","Lands in Jezero Crater.":"Jezero krateriga qo‘nadi.","Collects the “Sapphire Canyon” sample from “Cheyava Falls”.":"“Cheyava Falls”dan “Sapphire Canyon” namunasini oladi.","Potential biosignatures published in Nature.":"Ehtimoliy biosignaturalar Nature jurnalida e’lon qilinadi.","LECP instrument switched off to save power.":"Quvvatni tejash uchun LECP asbobi o‘chirildi.","Will be one light-day (about 25.9 billion km) from Earth.":"Yerdan bir yorug‘lik kuni (taxminan 25,9 mlrd km) uzoqlikda bo‘ladi.","Passes a marathon distance (42.2 km).":"Marafon masofasini (42,2 km) bosib o‘tadi.","Sets the off-world driving record.":"Boshqa sayyorada yo‘l bosish rekordini o‘rnatadi.","First extended mission begins.":"Birinchi kengaytirilgan missiya boshlanadi.","Claim, evidence, limits":"Da’vo, dalillar, cheklovlar","Every claim is labelled: ✓ an established finding, ≈ an interpretation, ? an open question. Open a record to see the evidence, its limits and the source.":"Har bir da’vo belgilangan: ✓ aniqlangan fakt, ≈ talqin, ? ochiq savol. Dalillar, cheklovlar va manbani ko‘rish uchun yozuvni oching.","Object":"Apparat","All objects":"Barcha apparatlar","Category":"Toifa","All categories":"Barcha toifalar","Established":"Aniqlangan","Interpretation":"Talqin","Unresolved":"Ochiq savol","✓ Established":"✓ Aniqlangan","≈ Interpretation":"≈ Talqin","? Unresolved":"? Ochiq savol","Laser ranging measures the Earth–Moon distance to within a few millimetres.":"Lazer lokatsiyasi Yer–Oy masofasini bir necha millimetr aniqlikda o‘lchaydi.","Evidence":"Dalillar","Laser pulses fired from observatories and timed on their round trip to the reflector arrays, for more than five decades.":"Observatoriyalardan yuborilgan lazer impulslari va ularning qaytargichlargacha borib-kelish vaqti — ellik yildan ortiq o‘lchovlar.","Limits":"Cheklovlar","The returns are extremely faint: in good conditions about one photon every few seconds.":"Qaytgan signal juda zaif: yaxshi sharoitda bir necha soniyada taxminan bitta foton.","Source":"Manba","The Moon is moving away from Earth by about 3.8 cm a year.":"Oy Yerdan har yili taxminan 3,8 sm uzoqlashmoqda.","Decades of lunar laser ranging.":"O‘n yilliklar davomida Oyni lazer bilan o‘lchash.","A long-term average; models keep refining it.":"Bu uzoq muddatli o‘rtacha qiymat; modellar uni aniqlashtirishda davom etmoqda.","The Moon has a fluid core.":"Oyning yadrosi suyuq.","Lunar laser ranging data, which showed this about 20 years before 2019.":"Oyni lazer bilan o‘lchash ma’lumotlari buni 2019-yildan taxminan 20 yil oldin ko‘rsatgan.","Indirect: worked out from how the Moon moves, not seen directly.":"Bilvosita: Oyning harakatidan xulosa qilingan, bevosita ko‘rilmagan.","Io, a moon of Jupiter, has active volcanoes.":"Yupiterning yo‘ldoshi Ioda faol vulqonlar bor.","Voyager 1 pictures from March 1979 showing volcanic plumes.":"Voyager 1 ning 1979-yil martidagi vulqon otilishlari ko‘rinadigan suratlari.","A flyby snapshot: later missions are needed to follow how the eruptions change.":"Yaqinidan uchib o‘tishda olingan surat: otilishlar qanday o‘zgarishini kuzatish uchun keyingi missiyalar kerak.","Voyager 1 left the heliosphere and entered interstellar space on Aug. 25, 2012.":"Voyager 1 2012-yil 25-avgustda geliosferani tark etib, yulduzlararo fazoga kirdi.","Its instruments measured the change from the Sun’s particles to the interstellar medium.":"Uning asboblari Quyosh zarralaridan yulduzlararo muhitga o‘tishni o‘lchadi.","Exactly where the boundary lies was debated at the time.":"Chegara aynan qayerdan o‘tishi o‘sha paytda munozarali edi.","A small wheeled rover can drive and do science on Mars.":"Kichik g‘ildirakli marsoxod Marsda yura oladi va tadqiqot olib bora oladi.","Sojourner drove about 100 m and worked 83 days against a 7-day plan.":"Sojourner taxminan 100 m yo‘l bosdi va 7 kunlik reja o‘rniga 83 kun ishladi.","One small rover at one landing site, never more than about 12 m from its lander.":"Bitta qo‘nish joyida bitta kichik marsoxod, qo‘nish modulidan taxminan 12 m dan uzoqqa ketmagan.","Running water once shaped the Ares Vallis landing site.":"Bir vaqtlar oqar suv Ares vodiysidagi qo‘nish joyini shakllantirgan.","Rounded pebbles and rocks that look like conglomerates.":"Silliqlangan shag‘al va konglomeratga o‘xshash toshlar.","Based on pictures and a few chemical analyses at a single site.":"Bitta joydagi suratlar va bir nechta kimyoviy tahlillarga asoslangan.","The silica-rich soil at Home Plate formed around hot springs or steam vents.":"Home Plate yonidagi kremnezyomga boy grunt issiq buloqlar yoki bug‘ chiqadigan joylar atrofida hosil bo‘lgan.","Spirit’s broken, dragging wheel exposed soil about 90% silica.":"Spiritning sudralib yurgan singan g‘ildiragi taxminan 90% kremnezyomdan iborat gruntni ochib berdi.","More than one hot-water setting fits the data; it is read by comparison with places on Earth.":"Ma’lumotlarga issiq suvli bir nechta muhit mos keladi; ular Yerdagi joylar bilan solishtirib talqin qilinadi.","Water at the “Comanche” outcrop was not acidic.":"“Comanche” qoyasi yonidagi suv kislotali bo‘lmagan.","Carbonates about ten times more abundant than in any Martian rock studied before.":"Karbonatlar avval o‘rganilgan har qanday Mars toshidagidan taxminan o‘n barobar ko‘p.","One outcrop; it does not tell how long the water lasted.":"Bitta qoya; u suv qancha vaqt turganini aytmaydi.","Liquid water once soaked Meridiani Planum.":"Bir vaqtlar suyuq suv Meridiani Planumni shimdirgan.","Hematite spherules (“blueberries”) and bright gypsum veins.":"Gematit sharchalari (“ko‘k mevalar”) va oq gips tomirlari.","That early water was acidic, which is hard on life.":"O‘sha dastlabki suv kislotali bo‘lgan, bu esa hayot uchun og‘ir sharoit.","Jezero Crater once held a lake and a river delta.":"Bir vaqtlar Jezero kraterida ko‘l va daryo deltasi bo‘lgan.","Delta layers imaged and sampled by the rover.":"Marsoxod suratga olgan va namuna olgan delta qatlamlari.","How long the lake lasted is still being worked out.":"Ko‘l qancha vaqt mavjud bo‘lgani hali aniqlanmoqda.","Was there ever microbial life on Mars?":"Marsda qachondir mikrob hayoti bo‘lganmi?","The “Sapphire Canyon” sample holds potential biosignatures (Nature, Sept. 2025).":"“Sapphire Canyon” namunasida ehtimoliy biosignaturalar bor (Nature, 2025-yil sentabr).","The same minerals can form without life. Confirming it needs labs on Earth, and sample return is not yet approved.":"Xuddi shu minerallar hayotsiz ham hosil bo‘lishi mumkin. Tasdiqlash uchun Yerdagi laboratoriyalar kerak, namunalarni olib kelish esa hali tasdiqlanmagan.","Why they went quiet":"Ular nega jim qoldi","Four short films made from NASA photographs, with narration and subtitles: what happened to each spacecraft that lost contact or had to slow down, and why.":"NASA suratlaridan tuzilgan, ovozli va subtitrli to‘rtta qisqa film: aloqani yo‘qotgan yoki cheklangan rejimda ishlashga majbur bo‘lgan har bir apparat bilan nima bo‘ldi va nima uchun.","Its lander’s battery failed":"Qo‘nish moduli batareyasi ishdan chiqdi","Sojourner: the rover that could not call home":"Sojourner: uyga qo‘ng‘iroq qila olmagan marsoxod","Stuck in sand before winter":"Qish oldidan qumga botib qoldi","Spirit: stuck before winter":"Spirit: qish oldidan botib qoldi","A dust storm hid the Sun":"Chang bo‘roni Quyoshni to‘sib qo‘ydi","Opportunity: the storm that hid the Sun":"Opportunity: Quyoshni to‘sgan bo‘ron","Its power is running out":"Uning quvvati tugab bormoqda","Voyager 1: running out of power, still talking":"Voyager 1: quvvati tugab bormoqda, lekin hali aloqada","How much do you know?":"Qancha bilasiz?","Three rounds: is it still working, the six missions, and the words of space exploration. Questions change every time you play.":"Uchta raund: u hali ishlaydimi, oltita missiya va koinot tadqiqotlari so‘zlari. Savollar har o‘yinda o‘zgaradi.","Three rounds. Every answer comes with the reason, and good scores unlock achievements.":"Uchta raund. Har bir javobga izoh beriladi, yaxshi natijalar esa yutuqlarni ochadi.","Working or existing?":"Ishlaydimi yoki shunchaki mavjudmi?","6 questions: which status label fits each object today":"6 ta savol: bugun har bir apparatga qaysi holat mos keladi","Not played yet":"Hali o‘ynalmagan","Missions round":"Missiyalar raundi","10 questions about the six objects":"Oltita apparat haqida 10 ta savol","Glossary round":"Lug‘at raundi","8 questions: match the word to its meaning":"8 ta savol: so‘zni ma’nosiga moslang","Your mission log":"Sizning missiya jurnalingiz","Six achievements for what you learn: the six objects, the films, the three test rounds and the glossary. Progress is saved in this browser only.":"O‘rgangan narsangiz uchun oltita yutuq: oltita apparat, filmlar, testning uchta raundi va lug‘at. Natija faqat shu brauzerda saqlanadi.","Grand tour":"Katta sayohat","Open the details of all six objects.":"Oltita apparatning hammasi haqida batafsil ma’lumotni oching.","Score 6 out of 6 in the status round.":"Holatlar raundida 6 dan 6 ball to‘plang.","Locked":"Yopiq","Mission specialist":"Missiya mutaxassisi","Score 9 or 10 in the missions round.":"Missiyalar raundida 9 yoki 10 ball to‘plang.","Word wizard":"So‘z ustasi","Score 8 out of 8 in the glossary round.":"Lug‘at raundida 8 dan 8 ball to‘plang.","Dictionary diver":"Lug‘at sayyohi","Open 10 different glossary terms.":"Lug‘atdagi 10 ta turli atamani oching.","Film buff":"Kinoshinavanda","Watch all four films to the end.":"To‘rtta filmning hammasini oxirigacha ko‘ring.","Side by side, with sources":"Yonma-yon, manbalari bilan","All six objects in one table, how the facts were checked, and every NASA page we used.":"Oltita apparat bitta jadvalda, faktlar qanday tekshirilgani va biz foydalangan barcha NASA sahifalari.","Compare: sections":"Solishtirish: bo‘limlar","Method":"Usul","Six objects side by side":"Oltita apparat yonma-yon","One row per spacecraft: when it left, where it is and whether it works. The full story of each is one click away.":"Har bir apparatga bitta qator: qachon uchgan, qayerda va ishlaydimi. Har birining to‘liq tarixi bir bosishda.","Spacecraft":"Apparat","Status today":"Bugungi holati","Sources":"Manbalar","Sea of Tranquility, Moon":"Osoyishtalik dengizi, Oy","It has no power and no moving parts, which is why it has lasted more than 55 years.":"Unda na quvvat, na harakatlanuvchi qism bor — shuning uchun u 55 yildan ortiq vaqtdan beri xizmat qilmoqda.","Interstellar space":"Yulduzlararo fazo","Two instruments are still on: the magnetometer (MAG) and the plasma wave subsystem (PWS).":"Hali ikkita asbob yoqilgan: magnitometr (MAG) va plazma to‘lqinlari asbobi (PWS).","Ares Vallis, Mars":"Ares vodiysi, Mars","It never went more than about 12 m from the lander, because it talked to Earth through the lander’s radio.":"U qo‘nish modulidan taxminan 12 m dan uzoqqa ketmagan, chunki Yer bilan modul radiosi orqali bog‘langan.","Gusev Crater, Mars":"Gusev krateri, Mars","Got stuck in soft soil on May 1, 2009.":"2009-yil 1-mayda yumshoq gruntga botib qoldi.","Endeavour Crater, Mars":"Endeavour krateri, Mars","In 2018 a dust storm covered the whole planet and blocked sunlight from its solar panels.":"2018-yilda chang bo‘roni butun sayyorani qopladi va quyosh panellariga tushadigan nurni to‘sdi.","Its driving systems are fully working.":"Uning harakat tizimlari to‘liq ishlamoqda.","Still there is not the same as still working":"Hali o‘sha yerda bo‘lish hali ishlash degani emas","Spirit and Opportunity are still on Mars, but they have been silent for years. Voyager 1 still works and sends data, but with only two of its ten instruments switched on.":"Spirit va Opportunity hali ham Marsda, lekin ko‘p yillardan beri jim. Voyager 1 hali ishlaydi va ma’lumot yuboradi, biroq uning o‘nta asbobidan faqat ikkitasi yoqilgan.","How the evidence stays honest":"Dalillar qanday halol qoladi","Label every claim":"Har bir da’voni belgilash","Established, interpretation or open question. Never blended together.":"Aniqlangan fakt, talqin yoki ochiq savol. Hech qachon aralashtirilmaydi.","Exists is not works":"Mavjud bo‘lish ishlash degani emas","Every object carries a status, because hardware stays long after it stops.":"Har bir apparatning holati bor, chunki texnika ishlashdan to‘xtagandan keyin ham uzoq qoladi.","NASA first":"Avval NASA","Each object links at least two primary sources. Figures that change are sent to the live NASA page.":"Har bir apparat kamida ikkita birlamchi manbaga havola beradi. O‘zgaradigan raqamlar uchun NASA’ning jonli sahifasiga yo‘naltiramiz.","Nothing invented":"Hech narsa to‘qib chiqarilmagan","No simulated telemetry, no made-up discoveries. Simplified 3D models and estimates are marked as such.":"Soxta telemetriya yo‘q, o‘ylab topilgan kashfiyotlar yo‘q. Soddalashtirilgan 3D modellar va taxminlar belgilangan.","About":"Loyiha haqida","About Singularity’s":"Singularity’s haqida","A student project about what NASA’s explorers leave behind, and how we know whether they still work.":"NASA tadqiqotchilari o‘zidan keyin nima qoldirishi va ular hali ishlashini qanday bilishimiz haqidagi o‘quvchilar loyihasi.","Why":"Nima uchun","Space missions end, but the hardware and the evidence stay. Singularity’s shows what six NASA explorers left behind and whether each one still works.":"Kosmik missiyalar tugaydi, lekin texnika va dalillar qoladi. Singularity’s NASAning olti tadqiqotchisi nimani qoldirganini va har biri hali ishlashini ko‘rsatadi.","For whom":"Kim uchun","School students who want to understand how we know what we know about the Moon, Mars and deep space.":"Oy, Mars va uzoq koinot haqida bilganlarimizni qayerdan bilishimizni tushunmoqchi bo‘lgan o‘quvchilar uchun.","Where the data comes from":"Ma’lumotlar qayerdan olingan","NASA and JPL mission pages, NASA’s 3D models and photographs, the JPL Horizons ephemeris and NASA’s live Perseverance feeds. Every claim links to its source.":"NASA va JPL missiya sahifalari, NASA’ning 3D modellari va suratlari, JPL Horizons efemeridalari va NASA’ning jonli Perseverance lentalari. Har bir da’vo o‘z manbasiga havola beradi.","How the facts were checked":"Faktlar qanday tekshirilgan","The team’s analyst collected the facts into one table on Oct. 22, 2026, from NASA pages only. Calculated figures are labelled as calculated, and the simplified 3D models as simplified.":"Jamoa tahlilchisi 2026-yil 22-oktabrda faktlarni faqat NASA sahifalaridan bitta jadvalga yig‘di. Hisoblangan raqamlar hisoblangan, soddalashtirilgan 3D modellar esa soddalashtirilgan deb belgilangan.","The team":"Jamoa","Team lead: Muzayana. Analyst, engineer and programmer: the team of four.":"Jamoa rahbari: Muzayana. Tahlilchi, muhandis va dasturchi — to‘rt kishilik jamoa.","The words of space exploration":"Koinot tadqiqotlari so‘zlari","Every special term used on Singularity’s, explained simply. Underlined words anywhere on the site open these explanations too.":"Singularity’sdagi barcha maxsus atamalar oddiy tilda. Saytning istalgan joyidagi tagiga chizilgan so‘zlar ham shu izohlarni ochadi.","Filter terms":"Atamalarni saralash","Filter terms…":"Atamani topish…","Jump to a letter":"Harfga o‘tish","Alpha Particle X-ray Spectrometer. Pressed against a rock, it measures which chemical elements the rock contains.":"Alfa-zarracha rentgen spektrometri. Toshga bosilganda u toshda qaysi kimyoviy elementlar borligini o‘lchaydi.","On Singularity’s:":"Singularity’sda:","Astronomical unit (AU)":"Astronomik birlik (a. b.)","The average distance between Earth and the Sun, about 149.6 million km. Mars orbits about 1.5 AU from the Sun; Voyager 1 is more than 170 AU away.":"Yer bilan Quyosh orasidagi o‘rtacha masofa, taxminan 149,6 mln km. Mars Quyoshdan taxminan 1,5 a. b. uzoqlikda aylanadi; Voyager 1 esa 170 a. b. dan ham uzoqda.","Biosignature":"Biosignatura","A pattern that life could have made. A potential biosignature, like the one in the rock “Cheyava Falls”, is a clue that needs more study, not proof of life.":"Hayot qoldirgan bo‘lishi mumkin bo‘lgan iz. “Cheyava Falls” toshidagi kabi ehtimoliy biosignatura — qo‘shimcha o‘rganish talab qiladigan belgi, hayot isboti emas.","Deep Space Network":"Uzoq koinot aloqa tarmog‘i","NASA’s giant radio dishes in California, Spain and Australia. Spread around the globe, they can always reach a distant spacecraft as Earth turns.":"NASA’ning Kaliforniya, Ispaniya va Avstraliyadagi ulkan antennalari. Ular yer shari bo‘ylab joylashgan, shuning uchun Yer aylanganda ham uzoqdagi apparat bilan doim bog‘lana oladi.","Ecliptic":"Ekliptika","The flat plane of Earth’s orbit around the Sun. The planets all orbit close to it; Voyager 1 flies about 35° above it.":"Yerning Quyosh atrofidagi orbitasi tekisligi. Barcha sayyoralar unga yaqin aylanadi; Voyager 1 undan taxminan 35° yuqorida uchadi.","Ephemeris":"Efemerida","A table of where a planet, moon or spacecraft is at given times. Singularity’s uses the JPL Horizons ephemeris for Voyager 1.":"Sayyora, yo‘ldosh yoki apparat ma’lum vaqtlarda qayerda ekanini ko‘rsatuvchi jadval. Singularity’s Voyager 1 uchun JPL Horizons efemeridalaridan foydalanadi.","Global dust storm":"Global chang bo‘roni","A Martian storm that can grow until it wraps the whole planet for weeks and blocks most of the sunlight. The 2018 storm ended Opportunity’s mission.":"Butun sayyorani haftalab o‘rab oladigan va quyosh nurining ko‘p qismini to‘sadigan darajada kuchayishi mumkin bo‘lgan Mars bo‘roni. 2018-yilgi bo‘ron Opportunity missiyasini yakunladi.","Golden Record":"Oltin plastinka","A gold-plated copper disc on each Voyager with sounds, music and pictures from Earth, a message for anyone who might find it.":"Har bir Voyager’dagi Yer tovushlari, musiqasi va tasvirlari yozilgan oltin qoplamali mis disk — uni topishi mumkin bo‘lgan har kimga xabar.","Gravity assist":"Gravitatsion manyovr","Flying close to a planet to borrow some of its speed. Voyager 1 used Jupiter and Saturn to speed up and change direction.":"Sayyora tezligining bir qismini “qarzga olish” uchun uning yaqinidan uchib o‘tish. Voyager 1 tezlashish va yo‘nalishni o‘zgartirish uchun Yupiter va Saturndan foydalangan.","Gusev Crater":"Gusev krateri","A crater about 160 km wide where Spirit landed in January 2004.":"Spirit 2004-yil yanvarida qo‘ngan, kengligi taxminan 160 km bo‘lgan krater.","Hazcam":"Hazkam","Hazard-avoidance cameras mounted low on a rover that watch for rocks and holes near the wheels.":"Marsoxodning pastki qismiga o‘rnatilgan, g‘ildiraklar yonidagi tosh va chuqurlarni kuzatadigan to‘siqlardan qochish kameralari.","Heliosphere":"Geliosfera","The huge bubble that the solar wind, the stream of particles from the Sun, blows around the Solar System. Voyager 1 crossed its edge in 2012.":"Quyosh shamoli — Quyoshdan chiqadigan zarralar oqimi — Quyosh tizimi atrofida hosil qiladigan ulkan pufak. Voyager 1 uning chegarasini 2012-yilda kesib o‘tgan.","Hematite":"Gematit","An iron-oxide mineral. Opportunity found tiny hematite spheres, nicknamed “blueberries”, that formed in water.":"Temir oksidi minerali. Opportunity suvda hosil bo‘lgan, “ko‘k mevalar” deb nomlangan mayda gematit sharchalarini topdi.","High-gain antenna":"Yuqori kuchaytirishli antenna","A dish that sends a narrow, strong radio beam. It has to point very precisely at Earth.":"Tor va kuchli radio nur yuboradigan likopcha. U Yerga juda aniq yo‘naltirilishi kerak.","The space between the stars, outside the Sun’s heliosphere. Voyager 1 was the first human-made object to reach it.":"Yulduzlar orasidagi, Quyosh geliosferasidan tashqaridagi fazo. Voyager 1 u yerga yetib borgan birinchi inson qo‘li bilan yaratilgan obyekt bo‘ldi.","Jezero Crater":"Jezero krateri","A 45 km crater on Mars that once held a lake fed by a river. Perseverance explores its old river delta and its rim.":"Marsdagi 45 km li krater, bir vaqtlar unda daryo to‘ldirib turgan ko‘l bo‘lgan. Perseverance uning qadimiy deltasi va chetini o‘rganmoqda.","Lander":"Qo‘nish moduli","A spacecraft that lands and stays in one place. Sojourner’s lander, Mars Pathfinder, carried the only radio that could reach Earth.":"Qo‘nib, bir joyda qoladigan apparat. Sojournerning qo‘nish moduli Mars Pathfinder Yerga yeta oladigan yagona radioni olib yurgan.","Light-time":"Yorug‘lik vaqti","How long light or a radio signal takes to travel a distance, at about 300,000 km every second. From the Moon it takes about 1.3 s; from Voyager 1 almost a whole day. A light-day is about 25.9 billion km.":"Yorug‘lik yoki radiosignal soniyasiga taxminan 300 000 km tezlikda masofani qancha vaqtda bosib o‘tishi. Oydan taxminan 1,3 soniya, Voyager 1 dan deyarli bir sutka. Bir yorug‘lik kuni taxminan 25,9 mlrd km.","Lunar laser ranging":"Oyni lazer bilan o‘lchash","Firing laser pulses at the reflectors on the Moon and timing the echo. It measures the Earth–Moon distance to a few millimetres and shows the Moon drifting away by about 3.8 cm a year.":"Oydagi qaytargichlarga lazer impulslarini yuborib, aks-sado vaqtini o‘lchash. U Yer–Oy masofasini bir necha millimetr aniqlikda o‘lchaydi va Oyning yiliga taxminan 3,8 sm uzoqlashayotganini ko‘rsatadi.","Magnetometer":"Magnitometr","An instrument that measures magnetic fields. Voyager 1’s sits on a 13 m boom so the spacecraft’s own magnetism does not disturb it.":"Magnit maydonlarini o‘lchaydigan asbob. Voyager 1 da u 13 m li shtangada joylashgan, shunda apparatning o‘z magnitizmi xalaqit bermaydi.","Meridiani Planum":"Meridiani Planum","A flat plain near the Martian equator where Opportunity landed in January 2004.":"Opportunity 2004-yil yanvarida qo‘ngan Mars ekvatori yaqinidagi tekislik.","An experiment on Perseverance that made oxygen from the carbon dioxide in Mars’ thin air, a test for future astronauts.":"Perseverance’dagi tajriba: u Marsning siyrak havosidagi karbonat angidriddan kislorod olgan — kelajakdagi astronavtlar uchun sinov.","Orbiter":"Orbital apparat","A spacecraft that circles a planet. Orbiters around Mars relay most rover data to Earth, because they have bigger radios and see Earth more often.":"Sayyora atrofida aylanadigan apparat. Mars atrofidagi orbital apparatlar marsoxodlar ma’lumotlarining ko‘p qismini Yerga uzatadi, chunki ularning radiosi kuchliroq va ular Yerni tez-tez ko‘radi.","Pale Blue Dot":"Xira ko‘k nuqta","The photo of Earth Voyager 1 took on Feb. 14, 1990 from about 6 billion km away: Earth is less than a single pixel in a sunbeam.":"Voyager 1 1990-yil 14-fevralda taxminan 6 mlrd km masofadan olgan Yer surati: Yer quyosh nurida bitta pikseldan ham kichik.","Prime mission":"Asosiy missiya","How long a mission is first designed and paid for. Spirit and Opportunity were planned for 90 sols; both lasted years longer.":"Missiya dastlab qancha muddatga loyihalanadi va moliyalashtiriladi. Spirit va Opportunity 90 solga rejalashtirilgan edi; ikkalasi ham yillar davomida uzoqroq ishladi.","Retroreflector":"Qaytargich","A device that sends light straight back to where it came from, whatever the angle. The Apollo 11 array has 100 corner-cube prisms of fused silica.":"Yorug‘likni qaysi burchakdan kelmasin, aynan kelgan joyiga qaytaradigan qurilma. Apollo 11 qaytargichida eritilgan kvarsdan yasalgan 100 ta burchakli prizma bor.","Rocker-bogie":"“Rocker-bogie” osmasi","A six-wheel suspension that lets a rover climb over rocks while keeping every wheel on the ground. Sojourner was the first to use it on Mars.":"Marsoxodga barcha g‘ildiraklarini yerdan uzmasdan toshlar ustidan o‘tishga imkon beradigan olti g‘ildirakli osma. Uni Marsda birinchi bo‘lib Sojourner ishlatgan.","Rover":"Rover (marsoxod)","A robot vehicle that drives across the surface of another world. All four Mars objects on this site are rovers.":"Boshqa sayyora sirtida yuradigan robot-mashina. Bu saytdagi Marsga oid to‘rtala apparat ham marsoxod.","RTG (nuclear power source)":"RITG (yadro quvvat manbai)","A radioisotope thermoelectric generator turns the heat of decaying plutonium-238 into electricity, day and night, with no moving parts. Voyager 1’s RTGs lose about 4 watts a year.":"Radioizotop termoelektrik generator plutoniy-238 parchalanishidan chiqqan issiqlikni kechayu kunduz, harakatlanuvchi qismlarsiz elektrga aylantiradi. Voyager 1 ning RITGlari yiliga taxminan 4 vatt yo‘qotadi.","Sample tube":"Namuna naychasi","Perseverance drills rock cores and seals them in tubes. Bringing some of them to Earth has been studied, but how and when is still being decided.":"Perseverance tosh kernlarini burg‘ulab, naychalarga muhrlaydi. Ularning bir qismini Yerga olib kelish o‘rganilgan, lekin qanday va qachon ekani hali hal qilinmoqda.","Silica":"Kremnezyom","Silicon dioxide, the stuff of quartz and glass. The nearly pure silica Spirit dug up forms around hot springs or steam vents, places where life thrives on Earth.":"Kremniy dioksidi — kvars va shisha moddasi. Spirit qazib chiqargan deyarli sof kremnezyom issiq buloqlar va bug‘ chiqadigan joylar atrofida hosil bo‘ladi — Yerda hayot gullab-yashnaydigan joylarda.","Sol":"Sol","A day on Mars: 24 hours, 39 minutes and 35 seconds. Rover teams count mission days in sols, starting with sol 0 on landing day.":"Marsdagi bir sutka: 24 soat 39 daqiqa 35 soniya. Marsoxod jamoalari missiya kunlarini sollarda hisoblaydi, qo‘nish kuni 0-sol hisoblanadi.","Solar panel":"Quyosh paneli","A panel that turns sunlight into electricity. Dust and the weak winter Sun ended the solar-powered Spirit and Opportunity.":"Quyosh nurini elektrga aylantiradigan panel. Chang va qishning zaif Quyoshi quyosh energiyasida ishlagan Spirit va Opportunity faoliyatini tugatdi.","Solar wind":"Quyosh shamoli","A constant stream of charged particles flowing out from the Sun at hundreds of kilometres per second.":"Quyoshdan soniyasiga yuzlab kilometr tezlikda oqib chiqadigan zaryadlangan zarralarning doimiy oqimi.","Spectrometer":"Spektrometr","An instrument that splits light or other radiation into its parts to work out what a rock or a gas is made of.":"Tosh yoki gaz nimadan iboratligini aniqlash uchun yorug‘lik yoki boshqa nurlanishni qismlarga ajratadigan asbob.","Telemetry":"Telemetriya","The data a spacecraft sends home about itself and its measurements: temperatures, power, position and science readings.":"Apparatning o‘zi va o‘lchovlari haqida uyga yuboradigan ma’lumotlari: harorat, quvvat, joylashuv va ilmiy ko‘rsatkichlar.","Team Singularity’s":"Singularity’s jamoasi","· Team lead: Muzayana · Analyst · Engineer · Programmer ·":"· Rahbar: Muzayana · Tahlilchi · Muhandis · Dasturchi ·","Team lead: Muzayana":"Rahbar: Muzayana","Analyst":"Tahlilchi","Engineer":"Muhandis","Programmer":"Dasturchi","About the project":"Loyiha haqida","Presentation mode":"Taqdimot rejimi","Singularity’s · team prototype, October 2026. Facts checked against NASA sources on Oct. 22, 2026. Images, 3D models and data: NASA/JPL-Caltech, NASA VTAD.":"Singularity’s · jamoa prototipi, 2026-yil oktabr. Faktlar 2026-yil 22-oktabrda NASA manbalari bilan solishtirilgan. Tasvirlar, 3D modellar va ma’lumotlar: NASA/JPL-Caltech, NASA VTAD.","Singularity’s is an independent student project, not affiliated with or endorsed by NASA. Status and figures change, so confirm them at the linked sources.":"Singularity’s — NASA bilan bog‘liq bo‘lmagan va u tomonidan tasdiqlanmagan mustaqil o‘quvchilar loyihasi. Holatlar va raqamlar o‘zgaradi, shuning uchun ularni havoladagi manbalardan tekshiring.","Back to top ↑":"Yuqoriga ↑","Enlarged photo":"Kattalashtirilgan surat","Close":"Yopish","Sound":"Ovoz","Off by default. Space ambience, shooting stars and button clicks.":"Odatda o‘chiq. Koinot foni, uchar yulduzlar va tugma ovozlari.","Background ambience":"Fon ovozi","The deep space hum and shooting stars":"Uzoq koinot shovqini va uchar yulduzlar","Button sounds":"Tugma ovozlari","Clicks, answers and achievements":"Bosishlar, javoblar va yutuqlar","Film narration":"Filmlarni ovozlash","Read the films aloud with your browser’s voice":"Filmlarni brauzer ovozi bilan o‘qib berish","Picture quality":"Tasvir sifati","3D models":"3D modellar","NASA’s 3D models you can turn and point at. Best on newer devices.":"Aylantirib, qismlarini ko‘rish mumkin bo‘lgan NASA 3D modellari. Yangi qurilmalarda yaxshiroq ishlaydi.","2D photos":"2D suratlar","NASA photos instead of 3D. Loads fast and runs smoothly on any device.":"3D o‘rniga NASA suratlari. Tez yuklanadi va istalgan qurilmada silliq ishlaydi.","Animation":"Animatsiya","Full":"To‘liq","Shooting stars and entrance effects.":"Uchar yulduzlar va paydo bo‘lish effektlari.","Reduced":"Kamaytirilgan","No moving effects: calmer and lighter for slow devices.":"Harakatlanuvchi effektlarsiz: sekin qurilmalar uchun osoyishtaroq va yengilroq.","Reload to apply":"Qo‘llash uchun qayta yuklash","Reset achievements":"Yutuqlarni tiklash","Presentation mode (P)":"Taqdimot rejimi (P)","Search Singularity’s":"Singularity’s bo‘yicha qidiruv","Search spacecraft, facts, words…":"Apparatlar, faktlar, so‘zlarni qidiring…","Search":"Qidiruv","Close search":"Qidiruvni yopish","Keywords":"Kalit so‘zlar","Moon":"Oy","laser":"lazer","retroreflector":"qaytargich","passive":"passiv","Earth–Moon distance":"Yer–Oy masofasi","interstellar":"yulduzlararo","nuclear power":"yadro energiyasi","Jupiter":"Yupiter","Saturn":"Saturn","heliosphere":"geliosfera","deep space":"uzoq koinot","Mars":"Mars","rover":"marsoxod","lander":"qo‘nish moduli","first rover":"birinchi marsoxod","solar power":"quyosh energiyasi","silica":"kremnezyom","stuck in sand":"qumga botgan","winter":"qish","dust storm":"chang bo‘roni","hematite":"gematit","record drive":"yo‘l rekordi","samples":"namunalar","biosignature":"biosignatura","active":"faol","Results":"Natijalar","Nothing found. Try another word, or a keyword such as #Mars.":"Hech narsa topilmadi. Boshqa so‘zni yoki #Mars kabi kalit so‘zni sinab ko‘ring.","↑ ↓ to move":"↑ ↓ — harakatlanish","Enter to open":"Enter — ochish","Ctrl K or / to search from anywhere":"Ctrl K yoki / — istalgan joydan qidirish","Close film":"Filmni yopish","Animated film. The narration is shown as subtitles below the picture.":"Film. Ovozli matn tasvir ostida subtitr sifatida ko‘rsatiladi.","Play film":"Filmni ko‘rish","Watch again":"Qayta ko‘rish","Position in the film":"Filmdagi joy","Narration on":"Ovozlash yoqiq","Narration off":"Ovozlash o‘chiq","Close presentation":"Taqdimotni yopish","← Back":"← Orqaga","Next →":"Keyingi →","Buzz Aldrin on the Moon beside the seismometer and the laser reflector, with the flag and the Lunar Module behind":"Bazz Oldrin Oyda seysmometr va lazer qaytargichi yonida, orqasida bayroq va oy moduli","LASER REFLECTOR · ON THE MOON SINCE 1969":"LAZER QAYTARGICHI · 1969-YILDAN BERI OYDA","A panel of 100 glass corner cubes that Neil Armstrong and Buzz Aldrin left on the Moon. It needs no power, and observatories still fire lasers at it to time the Earth–Moon distance to within a few millimetres.":"Nil Armstrong va Bazz Oldrin Oyda qoldirgan 100 ta shisha burchakli prizmadan iborat panel. Unga quvvat kerak emas, observatoriyalar esa Yer–Oy masofasini bir necha millimetr aniqlikda o‘lchash uchun unga hali ham lazer yuboradi.","glass corner cubes":"shisha burchakli prizma","the Moon moves away each year":"Oy har yili shuncha uzoqlashadi","power it needs":"unga kerak bo‘lgan quvvat","55+ years":"55+ yil","still in use":"va hali ham foydalanilmoqda","Built to":"Nima uchun qurilgan","Send laser pulses from Earth straight back to where they came from, so observatories can time the round trip and measure the distance to the Moon.":"Yerdan kelgan lazer impulslarini aynan kelgan joyiga qaytarish, shunda observatoriyalar borib-kelish vaqtini o‘lchab, Oygacha masofani aniqlay oladi.","What it found":"U nimani aniqladi","The Moon is moving away from Earth by about 3.8 cm (1.5 in) a year.":"Oy Yerdan har yili taxminan 3,8 sm uzoqlashmoqda.","The Moon has a fluid core, although scientists had expected a cool, solid one.":"Oyning yadrosi suyuq, garchi olimlar uni sovuq va qattiq deb kutgan bo‘lsa ham.","Gravity passes a test of Einstein’s ideas: the Sun pulls on Earth and the Moon in the same way, even though Earth contains more iron.":"Gravitatsiya Eynshteyn g‘oyalari sinovidan o‘tadi: Quyosh Yer va Oyni bir xil tortadi, garchi Yerda temir ko‘proq bo‘lsa ham.","The Earth–Moon distance is now measured to within a few millimetres.":"Yer–Oy masofasi hozir bir necha millimetr aniqlikda o‘lchanadi.","Four telescopes, in New Mexico, France, Italy and Germany, fire lasers at the Apollo arrays.":"To‘rtta teleskop — Nyu-Meksiko, Fransiya, Italiya va Germaniyada — Apollo qaytargichlariga lazer yuboradi.","Limits: the reflector is far too small to see from Earth, and by the time the laser reaches the Moon the beam is several kilometres wide.":"Cheklovlar: qaytargich Yerdan ko‘rish uchun juda kichik, lazer Oyga yetganda esa nur bir necha kilometr kenglikka yetadi.","The light that comes back is extremely faint: in good conditions about one photon every few seconds, so only a few observatories can do this.":"Qaytgan yorug‘lik juda zaif: yaxshi sharoitda bir necha soniyada taxminan bitta foton, shuning uchun buni faqat bir nechta observatoriya qila oladi.","The Apollo 11 Lunar Module standing on the grey lunar surface, with the Sun behind it":"Apollo 11 oy moduli kulrang Oy sirtida, orqasida Quyosh","The Lunar Module Eagle on the Sea of Tranquility. The reflector was set up a short walk away.":"Osoyishtalik dengizidagi Eagle oy moduli. Qaytargich undan bir necha qadam narida o‘rnatilgan.","Parts you can point at":"Ko‘rsatish mumkin bo‘lgan qismlar","Move the mouse over the 3D model, or tap it, to see these on the spacecraft. This model is a simplified Singularity’s build from NASA dimensions.":"Bu qismlarni apparatda ko‘rish uchun sichqonchani 3D model ustiga olib boring yoki unga teging. Bu NASA o‘lchamlari bo‘yicha Singularity’s yasagan soddalashtirilgan model.","Move the mouse over the 3D model, or tap it, to see these on the spacecraft.":"Bu qismlarni apparatda ko‘rish uchun sichqonchani 3D model ustiga olib boring yoki unga teging.","Corner-cube array":"Burchakli prizmalar bloki","100 fused-silica prisms, each 3.8 cm across. Each one sends light straight back to where it came from.":"Eritilgan kvarsdan yasalgan 100 ta prizma, har biri 3,8 sm. Har biri yorug‘likni aynan kelgan joyiga qaytaradi.","Aluminium panel":"Alyuminiy panel","46 × 46 cm, tilted toward Earth, which hangs high in the sky above Tranquility Base.":"46 × 46 sm, Osoyishtalik bazasi ustida osmonda baland turgan Yerga qaratib egilgan.","Pallet and legs":"Asos va oyoqlar","Carried out of the Lunar Module and set down by Buzz Aldrin in July 1969. No power, no moving parts, nothing to wear out.":"1969-yil iyulida Bazz Oldrin oy modulidan olib chiqib o‘rnatgan. Quvvatsiz, harakatlanuvchi qismlarsiz — eskiradigan narsa yo‘q.","Laser pulse from Earth":"Yerdan kelgan lazer impulsi","Observatories fire short laser pulses at the array. The round trip takes about 2.5 seconds and only a few photons come back.":"Observatoriyalar qaytargichga qisqa lazer impulslarini yuboradi. Borib-kelish taxminan 2,5 soniya davom etadi va faqat bir nechta foton qaytadi.","Other spacecraft":"Boshqa apparatlar","simplified model built by Singularity’s from NASA dimensions (not an official NASA model)":"NASA o‘lchamlari bo‘yicha Singularity’s yasagan soddalashtirilgan model (NASA’ning rasmiy modeli emas)","Illustration of the Voyager 1 spacecraft with its large dish antenna, entering interstellar space":"Illyustratsiya: katta likopcha antennali Voyager 1 apparati yulduzlararo fazoga kirmoqda","SPACE PROBE · IN FLIGHT SINCE 1977":"KOSMIK ZOND · 1977-YILDAN BERI PARVOZDA","After flying past Jupiter and Saturn, it became the first spacecraft to leave the heliosphere, in 2012. It is still sending data from interstellar space, though only two of its ten instruments remain on.":"Yupiter va Saturn yonidan uchib o‘tib, 2012-yilda geliosferani tark etgan birinchi apparat bo‘ldi. U hali ham yulduzlararo fazodan ma’lumot yubormoqda, biroq o‘nta asbobidan faqat ikkitasi yoqilgan.","Watch: why it is limited":"Ko‘rish: nega u cheklangan","Watch: why it went silent":"Ko‘rish: nega u jim qoldi","launched":"uchirilgan","instruments still on":"asbob hali yoqilgan","power lost every year":"har yili yo‘qotiladigan quvvat","1 light-day":"1 yorug‘lik kuni","away from Earth on Nov. 18, 2026 (expected)":"Yerdan uzoqlikda, 2026-yil 18-noyabr (kutilmoqda)","Fly past Jupiter and Saturn and study the two giant planets, their rings and their moons, including Saturn’s largest moon, Titan.":"Yupiter va Saturn yonidan uchib o‘tib, ikki ulkan sayyorani, ularning halqalari va yo‘ldoshlarini, jumladan Saturnning eng katta yo‘ldoshi Titanni o‘rganish.","Jupiter has a faint ring, and two moons nobody knew about: Thebe and Metis.":"Yupiterning xira halqasi va ilgari hech kim bilmagan ikki yo‘ldoshi bor: Fiva va Metida.","Its pictures from March 1979 showed volcanoes erupting on Io, a moon of Jupiter: the first active volcanoes seen beyond Earth.":"Uning 1979-yil martidagi suratlari Yupiterning yo‘ldoshi Ioda otilayotgan vulqonlarni ko‘rsatdi — Yerdan tashqarida ko‘rilgan birinchi faol vulqonlar.","Saturn has five more moons, a new ring, and small “shepherd” moons that keep some rings sharp.":"Saturnda yana beshta yo‘ldosh, yangi halqa va ba’zi halqalarni aniq shaklda ushlab turadigan kichik “cho‘pon” yo‘ldoshlar topildi.","Titan’s atmosphere is about 90% nitrogen and so thick it hides the surface completely.":"Titan atmosferasining taxminan 90% i azotdan iborat va u shunchalik zichki, sirtni butunlay yashiradi.","It is the first spacecraft to leave the heliosphere, the bubble of the Sun’s influence, so it measures interstellar space directly.":"Bu geliosferani — Quyosh ta’siri pufagini — tark etgan birinchi apparat, shuning uchun u yulduzlararo fazoni bevosita o‘lchaydi.","On Feb. 14, 1990 it took the “Pale Blue Dot”: Earth seen from about 6 billion km away.":"1990-yil 14-fevralda u “Xira ko‘k nuqta” suratini oldi: taxminan 6 mlrd km masofadan ko‘ringan Yer.","The low-energy charged particles instrument (LECP) was switched off on Apr. 17, 2026 to save power.":"Past energiyali zaryadlangan zarralar asbobi (LECP) quvvatni tejash uchun 2026-yil 17-aprelda o‘chirildi.","Its nuclear power sources (RTGs) lose about 4 W every year, so the team switches instruments off one by one.":"Uning yadro quvvat manbalari (RITGlar) har yili taxminan 4 Vt yo‘qotadi, shuning uchun jamoa asboblarni birin-ketin o‘chirmoqda.","The cameras have been off since 1990: no new pictures, only measurements.":"Kameralar 1990-yildan beri o‘chiq: yangi suratlar yo‘q, faqat o‘lchovlar.","A radio signal now takes almost a full day to reach Earth.":"Radiosignal endi Yerga deyarli bir sutkada yetib keladi.","Earth as a single faint bright dot inside a band of scattered sunlight against black space":"Qora koinot fonida tarqalgan quyosh nuri tasmasidagi bitta xira yorqin nuqta — Yer","“Pale Blue Dot Revisited”: Earth (the tiny dot in the light band) from about 6 billion km. Colours are false.":"“Xira ko‘k nuqta” qayta ishlangan: taxminan 6 mlrd km masofadan Yer (yorug‘lik tasmasidagi kichkina nuqta). Ranglar shartli.","A 3.7 m dish kept pointed at Earth. Its signal now takes almost a day to arrive.":"Doim Yerga qaratilgan 3,7 m li likopcha. Uning signali endi deyarli bir sutkada yetib keladi.","Ten-sided body":"O‘n qirrali korpus","Holds the computers and radios. Bolted to the outside is the Golden Record of sounds and pictures from Earth.":"Ichida kompyuterlar va radio asboblari. Tashqarisiga Yer tovushlari va tasvirlari yozilgan Oltin plastinka mahkamlangan.","Magnetometer boom":"Magnitometr shtangasi","A 13 m boom keeps the magnetometer away from the spacecraft’s own magnetism. MAG is one of the two instruments still on.":"13 m li shtanga magnitometrni apparatning o‘z magnitizmidan uzoqda ushlab turadi. MAG — hali yoqilgan ikki asbobdan biri.","Nuclear power sources (RTGs)":"Yadro quvvat manbalari (RITGlar)","Three plutonium generators on their own boom. They lose about 4 W a year, so instruments are switched off one by one.":"Alohida shtangadagi uchta plutoniy generatori. Ular yiliga taxminan 4 Vt yo‘qotadi, shuning uchun asboblar birin-ketin o‘chiriladi.","Science boom":"Ilmiy shtanga","Carried the cameras, switched off for good in 1990 after the Pale Blue Dot.":"Kameralarni olib yurgan, ular 1990-yilda “Xira ko‘k nuqta”dan keyin butunlay o‘chirilgan.","Active, 2 of 10 instruments on":"Ishlayapti, 10 ta asbobdan 2 tasi yoqilgan","The small Sojourner rover pressing its spectrometer against a large rock called Yogi":"Kichik Sojourner marsoxodi spektrometrini “Yogi” degan katta toshga bosmoqda","MARS ROVER · WORKED 1997":"MARSOXOD · 1997-YILDA ISHLAGAN","The first wheeled vehicle on another planet, about the size of a microwave oven. Planned for 7 days, it worked for 83, analysed the rocks around the Pathfinder lander and found signs that water once flowed there.":"Boshqa sayyoradagi birinchi g‘ildirakli mashina, taxminan mikroto‘lqinli pech kattaligida. 7 kunga mo‘ljallangan edi, lekin 83 kun ishladi, Pathfinder moduli atrofidagi toshlarni o‘rgandi va u yerda bir vaqtlar suv oqqani belgilarini topdi.","rover mass":"marsoxod massasi","worked, against 7 planned":"ishladi, rejadagi 7 kun o‘rniga","driven in total":"jami bosib o‘tilgan","pictures it took":"olingan suratlar","Show that a small wheeled rover can drive and do science on Mars, and that a low-cost landing on airbags works. Its spectrometer (APXS) measured what the nearby rocks and soil were made of.":"Kichik g‘ildirakli marsoxod Marsda yura olishi va tadqiqot olib borishi, havo yostiqlarida arzon qo‘nish esa ishlashini ko‘rsatish. Uning spektrometri (APXS) yaqin atrofdagi tosh va grunt nimadan iboratligini o‘lchadi.","It became the first wheeled vehicle on another planet.":"U boshqa sayyoradagi birinchi g‘ildirakli mashina bo‘ldi.","Rounded pebbles and rocks that look like conglomerates: running water once shaped the landing site, so ancient Mars was warmer and wetter.":"Silliqlangan shag‘al va konglomeratga o‘xshash toshlar: qo‘nish joyini bir vaqtlar oqar suv shakllantirgan, demak qadimiy Mars issiqroq va namroq bo‘lgan.","Dust in the Martian air is magnetic, probably because of a mineral called maghemite.":"Mars havosidagi chang magnitli — ehtimol, maggemit degan mineral tufayli.","The mission watched dust devils and early-morning clouds of water ice.":"Missiya chang quyunlari va erta tongdagi suv muzi bulutlarini kuzatdi.","Its airbag landing was later used for Spirit and Opportunity.":"Uning havo yostiqlarida qo‘nish usuli keyinchalik Spirit va Opportunity uchun ishlatilgan.","The last data came on Sept. 27, 1997, when contact with the lander was lost.":"Oxirgi ma’lumot 1997-yil 27-sentabrda, qo‘nish moduli bilan aloqa uzilganda keldi.","It lasted 12 times longer than planned.":"U rejalashtirilganidan 12 marta uzoqroq ishladi.","The rover is still physically on Mars, in Ares Vallis.":"Marsoxod hali ham Marsda, Ares vodiysida turibdi.","The Mars Pathfinder lander seen from above on orange Martian ground, its three solar petals open among deflated airbags":"Mars Pathfinder qo‘nish moduli yuqoridan to‘q sariq Mars gruntida, uning uchta quyosh yaprog‘i puchaygan yostiqlar orasida ochilgan","The Mars Pathfinder lander on Mars, its petals open among the deflated airbags. Sojourner drove off it down a ramp.":"Marsdagi Mars Pathfinder qo‘nish moduli, uning yaproqlari puchaygan yostiqlar orasida ochilgan. Sojourner undan trap orqali tushgan.","Its main power came from 0.2 m² of solar cells on the roof.":"Asosiy quvvatni tomdagi 0,2 m² quyosh elementlari bergan.","Front cameras":"Old kameralar","A stereo pair, with laser stripes to judge how tall the rocks ahead were.":"Oldindagi toshlar balandligini baholash uchun lazer chiziqli stereo juftlik.","Six 13 cm wheels":"Oltita 13 sm li g‘ildirak","On a rocker-bogie suspension, the idea later used by Spirit, Opportunity and Perseverance.":"“Rocker-bogie” osmasida — bu g‘oyani keyinchalik Spirit, Opportunity va Perseverance ishlatgan.","APXS spectrometer":"APXS spektrometri","Pressed against rocks such as “Yogi” to measure which chemical elements they contain.":"Qaysi kimyoviy elementlar borligini o‘lchash uchun “Yogi” kabi toshlarga bosilgan.","Radio antenna":"Radio antenna","Talked to the lander, never to Earth directly, which is why it stayed within about 12 m of it.":"Yer bilan emas, qo‘nish moduli bilan bog‘langan, shuning uchun undan taxminan 12 m ichida qolgan.","Warm electronics box":"Issiq elektronika bo‘limi","10.6 kg in total: the whole rover was about the size of a microwave oven.":"Jami 10,6 kg: butun marsoxod taxminan mikroto‘lqinli pech kattaligida edi.","Mission ended 1997":"Missiya 1997-yilda yakunlangan","Spirit rover’s solar-panel deck seen from above, lightly coated in dust":"Spirit marsoxodining quyosh panellari yuqoridan, biroz chang bosgan","MARS ROVER · WORKED 2004–2010":"MARSOXOD · 2004–2010-YILLARDA ISHLAGAN","Built for a 90-day mission in Gusev Crater, it worked for more than six years. Its stuck wheel dug up nearly pure silica, the kind that forms around hot springs, a sign of a much wetter ancient Mars.":"Gusev kraterida 90 kunlik missiya uchun qurilgan, lekin olti yildan ortiq ishladi. Uning tiqilib qolgan g‘ildiragi issiq buloqlar atrofida hosil bo‘ladigan deyarli sof kremnezyomni qazib chiqardi — bu qadimiy Mars ancha nam bo‘lganining belgisi.","planned mission":"rejalashtirilgan missiya","6 yr 2 mo":"6 yil 2 oy","actually worked":"aslida ishladi","driven":"bosib o‘tilgan","longer than planned":"rejadagidan uzoqroq","Study rocks and soil in Gusev Crater and look for clues that water once flowed there. The mission was planned for 90 Martian days.":"Gusev kraterida tosh va gruntni o‘rganish hamda u yerda bir vaqtlar suv oqqani belgilarini izlash. Missiya 90 Mars kuniga rejalashtirilgan edi.","In the Columbia Hills: bedrock of many kinds, some of it changed by water.":"Kolumbiya tepaliklarida: ko‘p turdagi tub jinslar, ularning bir qismi suv ta’sirida o‘zgargan.","At “Home Plate”: traces of an ancient volcano and explosive eruptions driven by hot underground water.":"“Home Plate” yonida: qadimiy vulqon va issiq yer osti suvi qo‘zg‘atgan portlovchi otilishlar izlari.","In 2007 its broken, dragging wheel dug up soil that was about 90% pure silica. On Earth this forms at hot springs and steam vents, so ancient Mars was much wetter.":"2007-yilda uning sudralib yurgan singan g‘ildiragi taxminan 90% sof kremnezyomdan iborat gruntni ochdi. Yerda bunday modda issiq buloqlar va bug‘ chiqadigan joylarda hosil bo‘ladi, demak qadimiy Mars ancha nam bo‘lgan.","In the “Comanche” rocks: about ten times more carbonate than in any Martian rock studied before, a sign of water that was not acidic and could have suited life.":"“Comanche” toshlarida: avval o‘rganilgan har qanday Mars toshidagidan taxminan o‘n barobar ko‘p karbonat — kislotali bo‘lmagan va hayot uchun mos bo‘lishi mumkin bo‘lgan suvning belgisi.","In 2005 it filmed dust devils moving across the plains.":"2005-yilda tekislik bo‘ylab harakatlanayotgan chang quyunlarini suratga oldi.","Last contact on Mar. 22, 2010. Most likely the Martian winter grew too cold for its heaters.":"Oxirgi aloqa — 2010-yil 22-mart. Ehtimol, Mars qishi uning isitgichlari uchun haddan tashqari sovuq bo‘lib ketgan.","The rover is still physically on Mars, next to Home Plate.":"Marsoxod hali ham Marsda, Home Plate yonida turibdi.","Pancam mast":"Pancam kameralari machtasi","Colour panoramic cameras and navigation cameras on a mast about as tall as a person.":"Odam bo‘yidek balandlikdagi machtada rangli panorama va navigatsiya kameralari.","Solar panels":"Quyosh panellari","They powered it for six years; the cold, dim Martian winter of 2009 to 2010 was too much.":"Ular uni olti yil quvvat bilan ta’minladi; 2009–2010-yillardagi sovuq va qorong‘i Mars qishi esa juda og‘ir keldi.","A steerable dish for talking straight to Earth.":"Yer bilan to‘g‘ridan-to‘g‘ri bog‘lanish uchun buriladigan likopcha.","Robotic arm":"Robot qo‘l","Carries a microscopic imager, two spectrometers and a tool that ground into rocks to see inside them.":"Mikroskopik kamera, ikkita spektrometr va toshlar ichini ko‘rish uchun ularni qirib ochadigan asbobni olib yuradi.","Six wheels":"Oltita g‘ildirak","Its right-front wheel stopped turning in 2006. Dragging it is how Spirit dug up nearly pure silica.":"Uning o‘ng old g‘ildiragi 2006-yilda aylanmay qoldi. Spirit aynan uni sudrab, deyarli sof kremnezyomni qazib chiqargan.","Keeps the computer and batteries warm through freezing Martian nights.":"Kompyuter va batareyalarni sovuq Mars kechalarida iliq saqlaydi.","Mission ended 2011":"Missiya 2011-yilda yakunlangan","Opportunity rover self-portrait with clean solar panels on the reddish Martian surface":"Opportunity marsoxodining toza quyosh panellari bilan qizg‘ish Mars sirtidagi avtoportreti","MARS ROVER · WORKED 2004–2018":"MARSOXOD · 2004–2018-YILLARDA ISHLAGAN","Planned for 90 days, it explored Meridiani Planum for almost 15 years and drove 45 km. Hematite spherules and gypsum veins it found showed that liquid water once flowed on Mars.":"90 kunga mo‘ljallangan bo‘lsa-da, u deyarli 15 yil Meridiani Planumni o‘rgandi va 45 km yo‘l bosdi. U topgan gematit sharchalari va gips tomirlari Marsda bir vaqtlar suyuq suv oqqanini ko‘rsatdi.","~15 years":"~15 yil","steepest slope climbed":"chiqqan eng tik qiyaligi","Find places on Mars where conditions may once have suited life, and look for signs of past water. The plan was 90 Martian days and 1 km of driving.":"Marsda sharoit bir vaqtlar hayot uchun mos bo‘lgan bo‘lishi mumkin joylarni topish va qadimgi suv izlarini izlash. Reja — 90 Mars kuni va 1 km yo‘l.","Small round grains of hematite, nicknamed “blueberries”. This mineral usually forms in water, but that water was acidic, which is hard on life.":"“Ko‘k mevalar” deb nomlangan kichik yumaloq gematit donalari. Bu mineral odatda suvda hosil bo‘ladi, lekin u suv kislotali bo‘lgan — hayot uchun og‘ir sharoit.","Bright veins of gypsum near Endeavour Crater, left by water flowing through cracks underground.":"Endeavour krateri yaqinidagi oq gips tomirlari — yer ostidagi yoriqlar bo‘ylab oqqan suv qoldirgan.","Clay minerals that formed in neutral water: the friendliest conditions for life of anywhere it went.":"Neytral suvda hosil bo‘lgan gil minerallari — u borgan barcha joylar ichida hayot uchun eng qulay sharoit.","In January 2005, an iron-nickel meteorite nicknamed “Heat Shield Rock”.":"2005-yil yanvarida — “Heat Shield Rock” deb nomlangan temir-nikel meteoriti.","Last contact on June 10, 2018.":"Oxirgi aloqa — 2018-yil 10-iyun.","Its 45.16 km driving record stood until Perseverance passed it on Oct. 11, 2026.":"Uning 45,16 km lik yo‘l rekordi Perseverance uni 2026-yil 11-oktabrda yangilaguncha saqlanib turdi.","The rover is still physically on Mars, in Perseverance Valley on Endeavour Crater.":"Marsoxod hali ham Marsda — Endeavour krateridagi Perseverance vodiysida turibdi.","In 2018 a dust storm that covered the whole planet blocked the sunlight they needed.":"2018-yilda butun sayyorani qoplagan chang bo‘roni ularga kerak bo‘lgan quyosh nurini to‘sib qo‘ydi.","They carried it 45.16 km, a record on another world until Perseverance passed it in 2026.":"Ular uni 45,16 km olib yurdi — bu Perseverance 2026-yilda yangilagunicha boshqa sayyoradagi rekord edi.","Mission ended 2019":"Missiya 2019-yilda yakunlangan","Perseverance rover selfie next to an arrowhead-shaped rock called Cheyava Falls":"Perseverance marsoxodining “Cheyava Falls” degan o‘q uchi shaklidagi tosh yonidagi selfisi","driven, a record":"bosib o‘tilgan, rekord","Martian days at the record":"rekord paytidagi Mars kunlari","rock samples collected":"yig‘ilgan tosh namunalari","extended mission end":"kengaytirilgan missiya tugashi","Look for signs of ancient microbial life in Jezero Crater, study whether Mars could support life, collect rock and soil samples for a possible trip to Earth, and help prepare for human missions.":"Jezero kraterida qadimgi mikrob hayoti izlarini izlash, Mars hayotni qo‘llab-quvvatlay olganmi — o‘rganish, Yerga olib kelish mumkin bo‘lgan tosh va grunt namunalarini yig‘ish va odamlar parvozlariga tayyorlanishga yordam berish.","Jezero Crater once held a lake, a river delta and rivers: a place that could have supported life.":"Bir vaqtlar Jezero kraterida ko‘l, daryo deltasi va daryolar bo‘lgan — hayot bo‘lishi mumkin bo‘lgan joy.","The crater floor is made of two kinds of volcanic rock that were changed by water.":"Krater tubi suv ta’sirida o‘zgargan ikki turdagi vulqon jinslaridan tashkil topgan.","A 2024 sample from the rock “Cheyava Falls”, named “Sapphire Canyon”, holds potential biosignatures (published in Nature, Sept. 2025). These are clues, not proof: the same minerals can also form without life.":"“Cheyava Falls” toshidan 2024-yilda olingan “Sapphire Canyon” namunasida ehtimoliy biosignaturalar bor (Nature, 2025-yil sentabr). Bu isbot emas, belgi: xuddi shu minerallar hayotsiz ham hosil bo‘lishi mumkin.","Its MOXIE experiment made oxygen from the carbon dioxide in Mars’ air.":"Uning MOXIE tajribasi Mars havosidagi karbonat angidriddan kislorod oldi.","Its microphones made the first recordings of sound on the surface of Mars.":"Uning mikrofonlari Mars sirtidagi tovushning birinchi yozuvlarini qildi.","On Oct. 11, 2026, its 2,006th Martian day, it passed Opportunity’s record: 45.22 km.":"2026-yil 11-oktabrda, o‘zining 2006-Mars kunida, u Opportunity rekordini yangiladi: 45,22 km.","Its first extended mission runs from October 2026 to about the end of 2028, along the crater rim and south toward “Rainbow Falls”.":"Uning birinchi kengaytirilgan missiyasi 2026-yil oktabridan taxminan 2028-yil oxirigacha — krater cheti bo‘ylab va janubga, “Rainbow Falls” tomon davom etadi.","Limits: the biosignatures can only be confirmed in labs on Earth, and the sample return is not yet approved. When it drives toward the Sun, glare in its cameras makes it park by mid-afternoon.":"Cheklovlar: biosignaturalarni faqat Yerdagi laboratoriyalarda tasdiqlash mumkin, namunalarni olib kelish esa hali tasdiqlanmagan. Quyosh tomon yurganda kameralardagi nur aksi uni kun yarmida to‘xtashga majbur qiladi.","View from orbit of reddish ridged Martian ground with faint rover tracks and a tiny rover":"Orbitadan qizg‘ish, qirrali Mars gruntining ko‘rinishi: xira iz va kichkina marsoxod","Seen from orbit on June 13, 2026 by the HiRISE camera: Perseverance is the small speck at the end of its tracks, a day before it passed the marathon distance.":"HiRISE kamerasi 2026-yil 13-iyunda orbitadan olgan surat: Perseverance — izlari oxiridagi kichik nuqta, marafon masofasini bosib o‘tishidan bir kun oldin.","Remote sensing mast":"Masofadan zondlash machtasi","Mastcam-Z, the zoom cameras, and SuperCam, which fires a laser at rocks to find out what they are made of.":"Mastcam-Z — zumli kameralar — va toshlar nimadan iboratligini bilish uchun ularga lazer otadigan SuperCam.","Robotic arm and turret":"Robot qo‘l va turel","A 2.1 m arm carrying the coring drill and the PIXL and SHERLOC instruments that studied “Cheyava Falls”.":"Kern burg‘usi hamda “Cheyava Falls”ni o‘rgangan PIXL va SHERLOC asboblarini olib yuradigan 2,1 m li qo‘l.","Sample handling":"Namunalar bilan ishlash","Inside the front of the body, a small inner arm seals rock cores into tubes for a possible return to Earth.":"Korpusning old qismidagi kichik ichki qo‘l Yerga olib kelish mumkin bo‘lgan kernlarni naychalarga muhrlaydi.","Nuclear power source (MMRTG)":"Yadro quvvat manbai (MMRTG)","Turns the heat of decaying plutonium into electricity, day and night, whatever the dust.":"Plutoniy parchalanishidan chiqqan issiqlikni chang qanday bo‘lmasin, kechayu kunduz elektrga aylantiradi.","The steerable dish that can talk to Earth directly; most data goes through orbiters overhead.":"Yer bilan bevosita bog‘lana oladigan buriladigan likopcha; ma’lumotlarning ko‘p qismi tepadagi orbital apparatlar orqali o‘tadi.","RIMFAX radar":"RIMFAX radari","Ground-penetrating radar that maps the rock layers beneath the rover as it drives.":"Marsoxod yurgan sari uning ostidagi tosh qatlamlarini xaritalaydigan georadar.","Front hazard cameras":"Old to‘siq kameralari","Cameras that watch for rocks and holes in front of the wheels.":"G‘ildiraklar oldidagi tosh va chuqurlarni kuzatadigan kameralar.","Wheels and rocker-bogie":"G‘ildiraklar va “rocker-bogie” osmasi","Six aluminium wheels on a suspension that keeps all of them on the ground; they have carried it more than 45 km.":"Barchasini yerda ushlab turadigan osmadagi oltita alyuminiy g‘ildirak; ular uni 45 km dan ortiq olib yurdi.","Rover body":"Marsoxod korpusi","The warm electronics box: computers, batteries, and MOXIE, the experiment that made oxygen on Mars.":"Issiq elektronika bo‘limi: kompyuterlar, batareyalar va Marsda kislorod olgan MOXIE tajribasi.","Correct.":"To‘g‘ri.","Next question":"Keyingi savol","See your score":"Natijani ko‘rish","Good start. Read the glossary and the mission windows, then try again.":"Yaxshi boshlanish. Lug‘at va missiya oynalarini o‘qib, qayta urinib ko‘ring.","Great work. A few more and you are an expert.":"Ajoyib ish. Yana ozgina — va siz mutaxassissiz.","Perfect score. Mission control is impressed.":"Mukammal natija. Parvozlarni boshqarish markazi hayratda.","Play again":"Yana o‘ynash","Without enough power to stay warm through the winter, it never woke up again.":"Qish bo‘yi isinish uchun quvvat yetmagach, u boshqa uyg‘onmadi.","Scientists are careful: such patterns can sometimes form without life.":"Olimlar ehtiyotkor: bunday izlar ba’zan hayotsiz ham hosil bo‘ladi.","Almost 12 times its plan.":"Rejadan deyarli 12 marta uzoqroq.","Engineers switch them off one by one to save power.":"Muhandislar quvvatni tejash uchun ularni birin-ketin o‘chirmoqda.","In June 2018 the storm blocked the sunlight its solar panels needed.":"2018-yil iyunida bo‘ron uning quyosh panellariga kerak bo‘lgan nurni to‘sdi.","Water once filled the crater and a river built a delta there.":"Bir vaqtlar kraterni suv to‘ldirgan va daryo u yerda delta hosil qilgan.","On Aug. 25, 2012 it crossed the edge of the Sun’s heliosphere.":"2012-yil 25-avgustda u Quyosh geliosferasi chegarasini kesib o‘tdi.","It is more than 25 billion km away, almost one light-day.":"U 25 mlrd km dan ham uzoqda — deyarli bir yorug‘lik kuni.","It lasts 24 h 39 min 35 s.":"U 24 soat 39 daqiqa 35 soniya davom etadi.","A record on another world for years, until Perseverance passed it.":"Perseverance yangilagunicha yillar davomida boshqa sayyoradagi rekord bo‘lib turgan.","It has no power at all, yet observatories still bounce lasers off it today.":"Unda umuman quvvat yo‘q, lekin observatoriyalar bugun ham undan lazer qaytaradi.","It still sends data from interstellar space, but only 2 of its 10 instruments are on.":"U hali ham yulduzlararo fazodan ma’lumot yuboradi, lekin 10 ta asbobidan faqat 2 tasi yoqilgan.","It is still on Mars, but contact ended on Sept. 27, 1997.":"U hali ham Marsda, lekin aloqa 1997-yil 27-sentabrda uzilgan.","It is still on Mars, stuck beside Home Plate; its last contact was in March 2010.":"U hali ham Marsda, Home Plate yonida botib qolgan; oxirgi aloqa 2010-yil martida bo‘lgan.","It is still on Mars; it went silent in a planet-wide dust storm in June 2018.":"U hali ham Marsda; 2018-yil iyunida butun sayyorani qoplagan chang bo‘roni paytida jim qoldi.","It is driving and collecting samples in Jezero Crater, on a mission extended to about 2028.":"U Jezero kraterida yuradi va namunalar yig‘adi; missiya taxminan 2028-yilgacha uzaytirilgan.","Open in the glossary":"Lug‘atda ochish","Open in the glossary →":"Lug‘atda ochish →","Voyager 1 from Earth":"Voyager 1 Yerdan","Perseverance has driven":"Perseverance bosib o‘tgan yo‘l","Every claim has a source":"Har bir da’voning manbasi bor","Six objects":"Oltita apparat","Film":"Film","Screen":"Ekran","NASA and JPL mission pages, NASA 3D models and photographs, the JPL Horizons ephemeris and NASA’s live Perseverance feeds.":"NASA va JPL missiya sahifalari, NASA 3D modellari va suratlari, JPL Horizons efemeridalari va NASA’ning jonli Perseverance lentalari.","Team Singularity’s · Team lead: Muzayana · Analyst · Engineer · Programmer":"Singularity’s jamoasi · Rahbar: Muzayana · Tahlilchi · Muhandis · Dasturchi","July 4, 1997. Mars Pathfinder lands in Ares Vallis, bouncing across the ground on giant airbags.":"1997-yil 4-iyul. Mars Pathfinder ulkan havo yostiqlarida sakrab, Ares vodiysiga qo‘nadi.","The petals open, and Sojourner, a rover the size of a microwave oven, rolls down a ramp onto Mars.":"Yaproqlar ochiladi va mikroto‘lqinli pech kattaligidagi Sojourner marsoxodi trap orqali Marsga tushadi.","But Sojourner had no radio strong enough to reach Earth. Every message went through the lander.":"Lekin Sojournerda Yerga yeta oladigan kuchli radio yo‘q edi. Har bir xabar qo‘nish moduli orqali o‘tardi.","It studied rocks the team named Yogi and Barnacle Bill. Planned for seven days, it worked for eighty-three.":"U jamoa “Yogi” va “Barnacle Bill” deb atagan toshlarni o‘rgandi. Yetti kunga mo‘ljallangan bo‘lsa-da, sakson uch kun ishladi.","On September 27, 1997, the lander fell silent. Its battery had worn out, and without it the lander could not survive the freezing nights.":"1997-yil 27-sentabrda qo‘nish moduli jim qoldi. Uning batareyasi eskirgan edi, usiz esa modul sovuq kechalarga bardosh bera olmadi.","Without the lander, Sojourner had no way to call home. It is still there in Ares Vallis, close to the lander that carried it.":"Qo‘nish modulisiz Sojourner uyga bog‘lana olmadi. U hali ham Ares vodiysida, o‘zini olib kelgan modul yonida turibdi.","Its idea lives on: every Mars rover since has six wheels on the same kind of suspension.":"Uning g‘oyasi yashamoqda: undan keyingi barcha marsoxodlarning oltita g‘ildiragi xuddi shunday osmada.","January 2004. Spirit lands in Gusev Crater, built for a mission of ninety days.":"2004-yil yanvar. Spirit Gusev krateriga qo‘nadi. U to‘qson kunlik missiya uchun qurilgan.","In 2006 its right front wheel stopped turning. Spirit learned to drive backwards, dragging the broken wheel.":"2006-yilda uning o‘ng old g‘ildiragi aylanmay qoldi. Spirit singan g‘ildirakni sudrab, orqaga yurishni o‘rgandi.","The dragged wheel scraped up almost pure silica, a sign that hot springs once bubbled here.":"Sudralgan g‘ildirak deyarli sof kremnezyomni qirib chiqardi — bu yerda bir vaqtlar issiq buloqlar qaynaganining belgisi.","In May 2009, at a place called Troy, its wheels broke through a crust into soft sand. Spirit was stuck.":"2009-yil mayida Troya degan joyda uning g‘ildiraklari qobiqni yorib, yumshoq qumga botdi. Spirit botib qoldi.","Engineers practised escape drives with a test rover in a sandbox on Earth. But winter was coming, and Spirit could not tilt its panels toward the low Sun.":"Muhandislar Yerdagi qum maydonchasida sinov marsoxodi bilan qutqarish harakatlarini mashq qildi. Lekin qish yaqinlashayotgan edi, Spirit esa panellarini past Quyoshga qarata olmadi.","Too cold and too weak to stay awake, Spirit went silent. Its last message arrived on March 22, 2010.":"Uyg‘oq qolish uchun juda sovqotgan va kuchsizlangan Spirit jim qoldi. Uning oxirgi xabari 2010-yil 22-martda keldi.","NASA listened for more than a year before ending the mission in May 2011. Ninety days had become six years.":"NASA missiyani 2011-yil mayida yakunlashdan oldin bir yildan ortiq tingladi. To‘qson kun olti yilga aylangan edi.","January 2004. Three weeks after its twin Spirit, Opportunity lands on Meridiani Planum.":"2004-yil yanvar. Egizagi Spiritdan uch hafta keyin Opportunity Meridiani Planumga qo‘nadi.","It found tiny grey spheres of hematite, nicknamed blueberries, that formed in water long ago.":"U uzoq o‘tmishda suvda hosil bo‘lgan, “ko‘k mevalar” deb nom olgan mayda kulrang gematit sharchalarini topdi.","Over fourteen years it drove forty-five kilometres, a marathon on another world.":"O‘n to‘rt yil ichida u qirq besh kilometr yo‘l bosdi — boshqa sayyoradagi marafon.","June 2018. A dust storm grows until it wraps the whole planet. Day turns into night.":"2018-yil iyun. Chang bo‘roni butun sayyorani o‘rab olguncha kuchayadi. Kun tunga aylanadi.","With almost no sunlight reaching its solar panels, Opportunity could not make enough power to keep talking.":"Panellariga deyarli quyosh nuri tushmagani sababli Opportunity aloqada qolish uchun yetarli quvvat ishlab chiqara olmadi.","Its last message came on June 10, 2018. Engineers sent more than a thousand commands, but no answer came back.":"Uning oxirgi xabari 2018-yil 10-iyunda keldi. Muhandislar mingdan ortiq buyruq yuborishdi, lekin javob kelmadi.","NASA ended the mission on February 13, 2019. It had been planned for ninety days. It lasted almost fifteen years.":"NASA missiyani 2019-yil 13-fevralda yakunladi. U to‘qson kunga rejalashtirilgan edi. Deyarli o‘n besh yil davom etdi.","September 5, 1977. Voyager 1 lifts off from Florida on a Titan rocket.":"1977-yil 5-sentabr. Voyager 1 Floridadan “Titan” raketasida uchadi.","It flies past Jupiter in 1979 and Saturn in 1980, using their gravity to speed on.":"U 1979-yilda Yupiter, 1980-yilda Saturn yonidan uchib o‘tadi va ularning tortishish kuchidan tezlashish uchun foydalanadi.","In 1990, from six billion kilometres, it looks back and takes the Pale Blue Dot: Earth, smaller than a pixel.":"1990-yilda olti milliard kilometr masofadan u ortiga qarab, “Xira ko‘k nuqta” suratini oladi: Yer bir pikseldan ham kichik.","In 2012 it leaves the heliosphere, the bubble of the solar wind, and becomes the first craft in interstellar space.":"2012-yilda u geliosferani — Quyosh shamoli pufagini — tark etib, yulduzlararo fazodagi birinchi apparatga aylanadi.","Out here sunlight is too weak for solar panels. Its power comes from plutonium generators, and they lose about four watts every year.":"Bu yerda quyosh nuri quyosh panellari uchun juda zaif. Quvvatni plutoniy generatorlari beradi va ular har yili taxminan to‘rt vatt yo‘qotadi.","To save power, engineers switch its instruments off one by one. Today only two of its ten are still on.":"Quvvatni tejash uchun muhandislar uning asboblarini birin-ketin o‘chirmoqda. Bugun o‘ntasidan faqat ikkitasi yoqilgan.","Its signal now takes almost a day to reach us. Giant dishes like these in Madrid still listen for it.":"Uning signali endi bizga deyarli bir sutkada yetib keladi. Madriddagi kabi ulkan antennalar uni hali ham tinglamoqda.","Which object has no power at all, yet is still used every year?":"Qaysi apparatda umuman quvvat yo‘q, lekin u hali ham har yili foydalaniladi?","It is a passive mirror: observatories fire lasers at it and time the echo.":"Bu passiv oyna: observatoriyalar unga lazer yuborib, aks-sado vaqtini o‘lchaydi.","How long does a laser pulse take to reach the Moon and come back?":"Lazer impulsi Oyga borib-kelishi uchun qancha vaqt kerak?","About 2.5 seconds":"Taxminan 2,5 soniya","About 0.25 seconds":"Taxminan 0,25 soniya","About 25 seconds":"Taxminan 25 soniya","About 4 minutes":"Taxminan 4 daqiqa","The Moon is about 384,000 km away; light covers that twice in roughly 2.5 s.":"Oy taxminan 384 000 km uzoqlikda; yorug‘lik bu masofani ikki marta taxminan 2,5 soniyada bosib o‘tadi.","What ended Opportunity’s mission?":"Opportunity missiyasini nima yakunladi?","A dust storm that covered the whole planet":"Butun sayyorani qoplagan chang bo‘roni","It got stuck in soft sand":"Yumshoq qumga botib qoldi","Its plutonium ran out":"Uning plutoniysi tugadi","How far did Opportunity drive on Mars?":"Opportunity Marsda qancha yo‘l bosdi?","Why did Spirit go silent in 2010?":"Spirit nega 2010-yilda jim qoldi?","Stuck in sand, it could not tilt its solar panels toward the winter Sun":"Qumga botgani uchun quyosh panellarini qishki Quyoshga qarata olmadi","A meteorite hit it":"Unga meteorit urildi","A dust storm buried it":"Uni chang bo‘roni ko‘mib yubordi","Its antenna broke off":"Uning antennasi sinib tushdi","What did Spirit’s broken, dragging wheel dig up?":"Spiritning sudralib yurgan singan g‘ildiragi nimani qazib chiqardi?","Nearly pure silica":"Deyarli sof kremnezyom","Ice":"Muz","Gold":"Oltin","A fossil":"Qazilma","Silica like this forms around hot springs: a sign of a wetter, warmer past.":"Bunday kremnezyom issiq buloqlar atrofida hosil bo‘ladi — nam va iliqroq o‘tmish belgisi.","How did Sojourner send its data to Earth?":"Sojourner ma’lumotlarini Yerga qanday yuborgan?","Through its lander’s radio":"Qo‘nish moduli radiosi orqali","Straight to Earth with its own dish":"O‘z antennasi bilan to‘g‘ridan-to‘g‘ri Yerga","Through an orbiter":"Orbital apparat orqali","It stored it to be collected later":"Keyin olib ketish uchun saqlab qo‘ygan","That is why it ended when the Pathfinder lander fell silent.":"Shuning uchun Pathfinder qo‘nish moduli jim qolganda u ham to‘xtadi.","Sojourner was planned for 7 days. How long did it work?":"Sojourner 7 kunga rejalashtirilgan edi. U qancha ishladi?","83 days":"83 kun","7 days":"7 kun","1 year":"1 yil","14 years":"14 yil","When did Voyager 1 enter interstellar space?":"Voyager 1 qachon yulduzlararo fazoga kirdi?","What powers Voyager 1?":"Voyager 1 ni nima quvvat bilan ta’minlaydi?","Plutonium generators (RTGs)":"Plutoniy generatorlari (RITGlar)","Batteries charged from Earth":"Yerdan quvvatlanadigan batareyalar","A small rocket engine":"Kichik raketa dvigateli","Sunlight is far too weak out there. The RTGs lose about 4 W a year.":"U yerda quyosh nuri juda zaif. RITGlar yiliga taxminan 4 Vt yo‘qotadi.","How many of Voyager 1’s ten instruments are still switched on?":"Voyager 1 ning o‘nta asbobidan nechtasi hali yoqilgan?","How long does Voyager 1’s radio signal take to reach Earth?":"Voyager 1 ning radiosignali Yerga qancha vaqtda yetib keladi?","Almost a whole day":"Deyarli bir sutka","About 8 minutes":"Taxminan 8 daqiqa","About 4 hours":"Taxminan 4 soat","About a week":"Taxminan bir hafta","What did Perseverance find in the rock “Cheyava Falls”?":"Perseverance “Cheyava Falls” toshida nima topdi?","Potential biosignatures: clues, not proof of life":"Ehtimoliy biosignaturalar: hayot isboti emas, belgi","Living bacteria":"Tirik bakteriyalar","Liquid water":"Suyuq suv","Nothing unusual":"Hech qanday g‘ayrioddiy narsa","Where is Perseverance exploring?":"Perseverance qayerni o‘rganmoqda?","Jezero Crater, an ancient lake bed":"Jezero krateri — qadimiy ko‘l tubi","The Sea of Tranquility":"Osoyishtalik dengizi","Olympus Mons":"Olimp tog‘i","Which was the first wheeled vehicle on another planet?":"Boshqa sayyoradagi birinchi g‘ildirakli mashina qaysi edi?","It rolled onto Mars in July 1997.":"U 1997-yil iyulida Marsga tushgan.","What is a sol?":"Sol nima?","A day on Mars":"Marsdagi bir sutka","A Martian year":"Mars yili","A unit of power":"Quvvat birligi","A type of rock":"Tosh turi","Mars Pathfinder":"Mars Pathfinder","Ares Vallis":"Ares vodiysi","Sojourner’s own view: its wheel, lower left":"Sojourner kamerasidan ko‘rinish: g‘ildiragi pastda chapda","The only link home":"Uy bilan yagona aloqa","rover → lander → Earth":"marsoxod → qo‘nish moduli → Yer","Days working":"Ishlagan kunlar","Planned":"Reja","Lander battery":"Modul batareyasi","January 2004: looking back at its lander":"2004-yil yanvar: qo‘nish moduliga ortga qarab","One wheel stuck: the drag marks":"Bitta g‘ildirak tiqilgan: sudralish izlari","The bright soil, 2007":"Oq grunt, 2007","Troy":"Troya","Soil churned by escape attempts":"Chiqishga urinishlardan titilgan grunt","Spirit’s power":"Spirit quvvati","January 2004":"2004-yil yanvar","Hematite “blueberries”":"Gematit “ko‘k mevalar”","Microscope view, a few millimetres each":"Mikroskop ostida, har biri bir necha millimetr","Distance driven":"Bosib o‘tilgan yo‘l","The storm seen from orbit":"Bo‘ron orbitadan","Sunlight":"Quyosh nuri","Power":"Quvvat","Commands sent":"Yuborilgan buyruqlar","Replies":"Javoblar","Cape Canaveral":"Kanaveral burni","January 1979":"1979-yil yanvar","November 1980":"1980-yil noyabr","Interstellar space (illustration)":"Yulduzlararo fazo (illyustratsiya)","Year":"Yil","Electrical power":"Elektr quvvati","Instruments on":"Yoqilgan asboblar","One-way light time":"Signalning bir tomonga vaqti","Why it went silent":"Nega u jim qoldi","Why it is limited":"Nega u cheklangan","Planned: 7":"Reja: 7","6 years":"6 yil","Planned: 90 days":"Reja: 90 kun","instruments still on · still sending data":"asbob yoqilgan · ma’lumot hali kelmoqda","Achievement unlocked":"Yutuq ochildi","Space ambience and shooting stars. Adjust it in Settings.":"Koinot foni va uchar yulduzlar. Sozlamalarda o‘zgartirish mumkin.","Lighter device detected":"Kuchsizroq qurilma aniqlandi","Use 2D photos instead of 3D models for smoother scrolling?":"Silliqroq aylantirish uchun 3D modellar o‘rniga 2D suratlardan foydalanilsinmi?","Use 2D":"2D ni yoqish","Keep 3D":"3D ni qoldirish","Saving mobile data":"Mobil trafikni tejash","Showing NASA photos instead of the 3D models (about 12 MB each).":"3D modellar o‘rniga NASA suratlari ko‘rsatilmoqda (har biri taxminan 12 MB).","Load 3D":"3D ni yuklash","Keep photos":"Suratlarni qoldirish","Progress reset":"Natija tiklandi","Your achievements start again.":"Yutuqlaringiz qaytadan boshlanadi.","Reset all achievements and progress on this device?":"Bu qurilmadagi barcha yutuqlar va natijalar tiklansinmi?","Fact":"Fakt","Quiz":"Viktorina","watched":"ko‘rilgan","Language":"Til","Click for its key facts":"Asosiy faktlar uchun bosing","Our planet · home of all six missions":"Bizning sayyoramiz · oltita missiyaning uyi","35° above the planets":"sayyoralardan 35° yuqorida","You are here":"Siz shu yerdasiz","Mercury":"Merkuriy","Venus":"Venera","Earth":"Yer","Uranus":"Uran","Neptune":"Neptun","Rocky planet · 1st from the Sun":"Toshli sayyora · Quyoshdan 1-chi","Rocky planet · 2nd from the Sun":"Toshli sayyora · Quyoshdan 2-chi","Rocky planet · 3rd from the Sun":"Toshli sayyora · Quyoshdan 3-chi","Rocky planet · 4th from the Sun":"Toshli sayyora · Quyoshdan 4-chi","Gas giant · 5th from the Sun":"Gaz giganti · Quyoshdan 5-chi","Gas giant · 6th from the Sun":"Gaz giganti · Quyoshdan 6-chi","Ice giant · 7th from the Sun":"Muz giganti · Quyoshdan 7-chi","Ice giant · 8th from the Sun":"Muz giganti · Quyoshdan 8-chi","A small, rocky world with a heavily cratered surface. It has almost no atmosphere and swings between extreme heat and cold.":"Sirti kraterlarga to‘la kichik toshli olam. Atmosferasi deyarli yo‘q, u yerda goh qattiq issiq, goh qattiq sovuq.","A dense carbon-dioxide atmosphere and thick clouds trap heat, making it the hottest planet in the Solar System.":"Zich karbonat angidrid atmosferasi va qalin bulutlar issiqlikni ushlab turadi, shuning uchun bu Quyosh tizimidagi eng issiq sayyora.","Our home world has liquid water on its surface and a nitrogen-oxygen atmosphere. It is the only world known to support life.":"Bizning ona sayyoramiz sirtida suyuq suv va azot-kislorodli atmosfera bor. Bu hayot borligi ma’lum bo‘lgan yagona olam.","A cold desert world with ancient river valleys, polar ice and the largest volcano known in the Solar System. Rovers study whether it was once habitable.":"Qadimiy daryo vodiylari, qutb muzlari va Quyosh tizimidagi eng katta ma’lum vulqonga ega sovuq cho‘l olami. Marsoxodlar u bir vaqtlar yashashga yaroqli bo‘lganmi — o‘rganmoqda.","The largest planet, a gas giant with huge storms such as the Great Red Spot. Its moon Io is the most volcanic world known.":"Eng katta sayyora, Katta qizil dog‘ kabi ulkan bo‘ronlarga ega gaz giganti. Uning yo‘ldoshi Io — ma’lum olamlar ichida eng ko‘p vulqonga ega.","Famous for bright rings made mostly of ice. Its moon Titan has a thick, mostly nitrogen atmosphere that hides its surface.":"Asosan muzdan iborat yorqin halqalari bilan mashhur. Uning yo‘ldoshi Titanning sirtini yashiradigan, asosan azotli zich atmosferasi bor.","An ice giant that spins on a strongly tilted axis. Methane in its atmosphere gives it a blue-green colour.":"Kuchli og‘gan o‘q atrofida aylanadigan muz giganti. Atmosferasidagi metan unga ko‘k-yashil rang beradi.","A distant ice giant with very fast winds and a deep blue colour.":"Juda tez shamollari va to‘q ko‘k rangga ega uzoqdagi muz giganti.","None of our six":"Bizning oltitamizdan hech biri","All six started here. The Apollo 11 reflector sits on its Moon.":"Oltitasi ham shu yerdan uchgan. Apollo 11 qaytargichi uning Oyida turibdi.","Sojourner, Spirit, Opportunity, Perseverance":"Sojourner, Spirit, Opportunity, Perseverance","Voyager 1 flew past in March 1979":"Voyager 1 1979-yil martida yonidan uchib o‘tgan","Voyager 1 flew past in November 1980":"Voyager 1 1980-yil noyabrida yonidan uchib o‘tgan","None of our six (Voyager 2 flew past in 1986)":"Bizning oltitamizdan hech biri (Voyager 2 1986-yilda yonidan uchib o‘tgan)","None of our six (Voyager 2 flew past in 1989)":"Bizning oltitamizdan hech biri (Voyager 2 1989-yilda yonidan uchib o‘tgan)","Loading…":"Yuklanmoqda…","Jezero Crater rim":"Jezero krateri cheti","western rim of Jezero Crater":"Jezero kraterining g‘arbiy cheti","NASA Mars Pathfinder mission pages and photographs":"NASA Mars Pathfinder missiyasi sahifalari va suratlari","NASA Mars Exploration Rover mission pages and photographs":"NASA Mars Exploration Rover missiyasi sahifalari va suratlari","NASA and JPL Voyager mission pages and photographs":"NASA va JPL Voyager missiyasi sahifalari va suratlari","Terms":"Atamalar"}};
